          "text": "<path>/home/stefan/dev/projects/triageflow/docs/handoffs/handoff-2026-06-13-ux-polish-phase1.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Handoff: UX Polish Phase 1 (AFK) Complete — Ready for Phase 2 (HITL)\n2: \n3: **Date:** 2026-06-13\n4: **Branch:** `master` (both repos)\n5: **Repo:** `psswid/triageflow-docs` (parent, incl. `backend/`) — commit `cb49b5e`  \n6: **Frontend repo:** `psswid/triageflow-frontend` — commit `e348c7c`\n7: \n8: ## Session Summary\n9: \n10: Implemented Phase 1 (AFK — Authoring From Keyboard) of Issue #11: UX Polish — Loading States, Error Recovery, Toast System. All 7 data-fetching components now use layout-matching skeleton loaders (replacing blank spinners), API errors are caught by ErrorFallback with retry wired to React Query refetch, and mutation errors trigger auto-dismissing toast notifications.\n11: \n12: ## What Changed — Reference Only\n13: \n14: Full details in these artifacts instead of duplicating here:\n15: \n16: | Artifact | Location |\n17: |----------|----------|\n18: | Implementation plan | `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-13-ux-polish-loading-errors.md` |\n19: | Session log | `raw_log.md` (entry: \"2026-06-13 — Issue #11: UX Polish\") |\n20: | Issue on GitHub | `psswid/triageflow-docs#11` (comment with Phase 1 summary) |\n21: | Plan file on GitHub | `psswid/triageflow-frontend#1` |\n22: \n23: **In brief:** 4 new components (Skeleton, ErrorFallback, Toast, ToastProvider), 10 files modified, +24 tests (frontend 119/119). Backend untouched. 2 code review issues fixed. End-to-end validation: frontend tests + TSC + ESLint clean, backend 242/242 + PHPStan clean.\n24: \n25: ## Phase 2 (HITL — Human In The Loop) Scope\n26: \n27: Phase 2 is a **human accessibility audit + design review**. The agent's role is to support the human reviewer by running the audit criteria — do NOT implement fixes without explicit sign-off.\n28: \n29: ### Components to Audit (9 pages)\n30: \n31: | Page | Component | Route |\n32: |------|-----------|-------|\n33: | Login | `LoginPage` | `/login` |\n34: | Register | `RegisterPage` | `/register` |\n35: | Verify Email | `VerifyEmailPage` | `/verify-email` |\n36: | Triage | `TriagePage` | `/triage` |\n37: | Triage Result | `TriageResultPage` | `/triage/result/{id}` |\n38: | Submissions List | `SubmissionsListPage` | `/submissions` |\n39: | Submission Detail | `SubmissionDetailPage` | `/submissions/{id}` |\n40: | Admin Dashboard | `DashboardPage` | `/admin` |\n41: | Admin Submission | `SubmissionDetailPage` (admin) | `/admin/submissions/{id}` |\n42: \n43: ### Audit Criteria\n44: \n45: ```markdown\n46: - [ ] Keyboard navigation: all interactive elements reachable via Tab\n47: - [ ] Focus indicators: visible focus ring on every interactive element\n48: - [ ] Semantic HTML: headings hierarchy (h1→h2→h3), landmarks (nav, main), lists where appropriate\n49: - [ ] ARIA labels: icons, loading states, dynamic content regions\n50: - [ ] Color contrast: WCAG AA minimum (4.5:1 normal text, 3:1 large)\n51: - [ ] Screen reader: announcements for dynamic updates, error messages\n52: - [ ] Touch targets: minimum 44×44px (mobile)\n53: - [ ] Motion: reduced-motion media query for animations\n54: - [ ] Design consistency: spacing/typography/color alignment with design system\n55: - [ ] Loading states: all Skeleton variants match their content layout\n56: ```\n57: \n58: ### Suggested Approach\n59: \n60: 1. Human reviewer opens each page in browser and runs through checklist\n61: 2. Agent supports by pointing to exact component files, line numbers, and Tailwind classes for each finding\n62: 3. Document findings in the issue or a shared doc\n63: 4. Human signs off on which fixes to implement\n64: 5. Only then should the agent implement Phase 2 fixes\n65: \n66: ## Project State\n67: \n68: | Repo | Branch | Status |\n69: |------|--------|--------|\n70: | `triageflow-docs` | `master` | Clean, pushed to origin |\n71: | `triageflow-frontend` | `master` | 15 commits ahead, pushed to origin |\n72: | `backend/` | (nested in docs repo) | No changes this session |\n73: \n74: ### To Run Locally\n75: \n76: ```bash\n77: # Backend (requires PostgreSQL via Docker)\n78: cd backend && symfony serve -d\n79: \n80: # Frontend\n81: cd frontend && npm run dev\n82: ```\n83: \n84: ## Suggested Skills for Next Session\n85: \n86: - **`ui-ux-pro-max`** → Load this skill before running the accessibility audit/design review. Contains the searchable design intelligence database for checking patterns against WCAG and design system best practices.\n87: - **`writing-plans`** → If the human signs off on a specific set of fixes that require multi-step implementation.\n88: - **`brainstorming`** → Before implementing any Phase 2 fixes that could affect UX or interaction patterns.\n89: - **`requesting-code-review`** → Before merging Phase 2 changes to verify audit criteria were properly addressed.\n90: - **`handoff`** → To save another handoff when Phase 2 is complete.\n\n(End of file - total 90 lines)\n</content>",
