          "text": "---\n\n### Question 10: Design system expansion.\n\nThe current theme has 3 primary shades + 4 urgency colors. That's enough for the functional triage tool. But the business pages (landing hero, feature cards, \"How It Works\" steps) need more visual vocabulary:\n\n| Missing | Why Needed |\n|---|---|\n| Secondary/accent color | Call-to-action buttons, highlights |\n| Neutral gray scale | Backgrounds, borders, muted text for legal pages |\n| Gradient or decorative elements | Landing page hero section |\n| Typography scale for marketing | Larger headings for hero text (text-4xl, text-5xl) |\n\nTwo approaches:\n\n| Approach | Description |\n|---|---|\n| **A: Extend the existing theme** | Add secondary-*, neutral-* tokens to `index.css`. One unified design system for both public and authenticated pages. |\n| **B: Separate visual identities** | Marketing pages get their own \"flashy\" styles. Authenticated pages keep the functional look. Two CSS files or Tailwind presets. |\n\nRecommendation: **A** — one unified system. The existing primary blue can be the foundation, add a warm accent (amber/gold or teal), and flesh out neutrals. The marketing pages use larger typography and more whitespace, but from the same token set.\n\nWhat accent color feels right? The sarcastic/AI theme suggests something energetic — amber/gold (warm, attention-grabbing) or teal (modern, clinical/medical vibe)?\n\n\n\n",
