                  "summary": "## Grill Session: Business Website Layer — 10 Questions Resolved\n\n**Context:** User wants to expand Issue #11 beyond accessibility audit into full business polish: public website pages, dark mode toggle, i18n (EN+PL), cookie consent, copywriting. Frontend is currently a pure authenticated SPA with zero public pages.\n\n### Codebase State Discovered (from explore subagent)\n- 10 routes, all behind auth; `/` redirects to `/triage`\n- No landing, about, legal, or contact pages\n- No i18n library, no cookie consent, no footer\n- Dark mode CSS exists (all components have `dark:` variants via Tailwind `@variant dark (&:where(.dark, .dark *))`) but zero JS control\n- Design tokens: only primary-50/500/900 + 4 urgency colors\n- 95 Vitest tests, TSC+ESLint clean\n\n### Decisions Resolved\n\n1. **Scope:** Issue #11 expanded to cover full business polish (not just accessibility audit)\n2. **Audience/Tone:** Sarcastic, self-aware, \"4th wall breaking\" — demo flex, not fake medical credibility. Landing page: \"Tired of waiting for your first-contact medical specialist? Let's hallucinate who can help you! (In case of real medical issue, please contact human specialist)\"\n3. **Page Inventory:** Landing (`/`), About (`/about`), How It Works (`/how-it-works`), Privacy (`/privacy`), Terms (`/terms`), Cookies (`/cookies`), Contact (`/contact` — links to piotrswiderski.dev) + existing auth pages\n4. **Layout Strategy:** Two layout wrappers — `MarketingLayout` (public, own header/footer) + `AppLayout` (authenticated, existing)\n5. **i18n:** `react-i18next` + `i18next-browser-languagedetector`. EN + PL. Browser detection (localStorage + navigator). All strings in JSON locale files organized by namespace (common, landing, about, howItWorks, legal, auth, triage, admin)\n6. **Backend:** Localized email templates for PL (Accept-Language header). No contact form backend needed.\n7. **Dark Mode:** System preference (`prefers-color-scheme`) + localStorage override. Single sun/moon toggle button. Not three-state.\n8. **Cookie Consent:** Bare-minimum notice — \"This demo uses browser storage for authentication and preferences. No tracking. No cookies. [OK, got it]\" — one click dismiss. No category toggles needed (zero tracking).\n9. **Accessibility Audit:** Deferred to follow-up issue. Build accessible-by-default (focus rings, semantic HTML, ARIA labels from Phase 1 patterns).\n10. **Design System:** Unified medical triage palette — primary: blue-600 (#2563eb), accent: teal-500 (#14b8a6), urgency: green→yellow→orange→red (existing), neutrals: slate-50 through slate-950. Typography scale expanded for marketing hero text.\n\n### CONTEXT.md Update\nAdded sentence noting frontend serves dual duty: authenticated SPA + public-facing business website with marketing pages. Core domain language unchanged (no new entities)."
