          "text": "## Design Review Complete — OpenFrontendSpecialist\n\nThe UI/UX Pro Max search generated a complete design system (Product Demo style, Glassmorphism, Poppins+Inter fonts) and the specialist identified **15 specific improvements** across all 7 pages and 5 shared components.\n\n### Critical Fixes (violate pre-delivery checklist):\n| # | Issue | Fix |\n|---|-------|-----|\n| 🔴 | Emoji icons (🤖⚛️🔄📊) in feature cards | Replace with Lucide SVG (`BrainCircuit`, `Layers`, `RefreshCw`, `BarChart4`) |\n| 🔴 | Zero mobile navigation — no hamburger menu | Add slide-in drawer to MarketingHeader |\n\n### Visual Polish (high impact):\n| # | Issue | Fix |\n|---|-------|-----|\n| 🟡 | About disclaimer uses alarming red | Change to amber (caution, not danger) |\n| 🟡 | Hero is plain text on gradient — no depth | Add frosted glass card (`backdrop-blur-xl`) |\n| 🟡 | No demo preview on landing | Add screenshot/browser-mockup section |\n| 🟡 | How It Works steps are stark | Add vertical timeline connecting line |\n| 🟡 | Contact page is one lonely link | Expand to 2×2 grid: Portfolio, GitHub, LinkedIn, Email |\n| 🟡 | Legal pages hard to scan | Add sticky Table of Contents sidebar (desktop) |\n| 🟡 | CTA colors inconsistent | Standardize: accent/teal for primary, primary/blue for secondary |\n\n### Design System Decisions:\n- **Typography:** Poppins (600/700) for marketing headings, Inter for body + UI. `pnpm add lucide-react` for icons.\n- **Glassmorphism:** Hero only — frosted card on gradient. Not on nav, footer, or legal pages.\n- **Dark mode hero:** `dark:from-primary-950` (deep navy) instead of `dark:from-gray-950` (flat dark).\n- **Tokens:** Add `--radius-*` series and `--font-heading`/`--font-sans`/`--font-mono` tokens.\n\n### Plan Impact:\nMost changes are **component tweaks** to pages already in the plan — Task 1 (tokens), Tasks 7-9 (pages), Task 4 (dark mode). New additions beyond the plan: Lucide icon import, mobile hamburger, demo screenshot placeholder, sticky ToC component, social link grid.\n\n---\n\n**Which of these design changes should I fold into the implementation plan before we begin building?** I recommend accepting all — they're all grounded in the design system search and none are scope-bloating. The plan already has the structural foundation for each.",
