            "output": "<path>/home/stefan/dev/projects/triageflow/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-13-business-website-layer.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Business Website Layer + i18n + Dark Mode Implementation Plan\n2: \n3: > **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.\n4: \n5: **Goal:** Transform the frontend from a bare authenticated SPA into a dual-purpose application: public-facing marketing website (landing, about, how-it-works, legal pages) + authenticated triage tool — with i18n (EN + PL), dark mode toggle, cookie consent, and a unified medical triage design system.\n6: \n7: **Architecture:** Two layout wrappers — `MarketingLayout` for public unauthenticated pages (with own header, footer, dark mode toggle, language switcher) and the existing `AppLayout` for authenticated pages. Both share a single `I18nProvider` (react-i18next), `ThemeProvider` (dark mode via system preference + localStorage override), and unified Tailwind design tokens. All pages translated via JSON locale files.\n8: \n9: **Tech Stack:** react-i18next, i18next-browser-languagedetector, react-helmet-async, lucide-react (icon system), Tailwind CSS 4, Poppins (Google Fonts headings), React Router 7, TanStack Query (existing), clsx (existing)\n10: \n11: ---\n12: \n13: ## File Structure Map\n14: \n15: ```\n16: src/\n17: ├── i18n/\n18: │   ├── index.ts                          # i18next initialization + browser detection\n19: │   └── locales/\n20: │       ├── en/\n21: │       │   ├── common.json               # Shared: buttons, nav, footer, errors\n22: │       │   ├── landing.json              # Landing page copy\n23: │       │   ├── about.json                # About page copy\n24: │       │   ├── howItWorks.json           # How It Works page copy\n25: │       │   ├── legal.json                # Privacy, Terms, Cookies pages\n26: │       │   ├── auth.json                 # Login, Register, Verify Email\n27: │       │   ├── triage.json               # Triage interview + result pages\n28: │       │   └── admin.json                # Dashboard, submissions, users\n29: │       └── pl/\n30: │           ├── common.json\n31: │           ├── landing.json\n32: │           ├── about.json\n33: │           ├── howItWorks.json\n34: │           ├── legal.json\n35: │           ├── auth.json\n36: │           ├── triage.json\n37: │           └── admin.json\n38: ├── hooks/\n39: │   ├── useAuth.ts                        # (existing)\n40: │   └── useDarkMode.ts                    # NEW: system pref + localStorage + toggle\n41: ├── components/\n42: │   ├── auth/\n43: │   │   └── AuthProvider.tsx              # (existing — add I18nProvider integration)\n44: │   ├── layout/\n45: │   │   ├── AdminRoute.tsx                # (existing)\n46: │   │   ├── AppLayout.tsx                 # (existing — add Footer)\n47: │   │   ├── Header.tsx                    # (existing — add i18n)\n48: │   │   ├── ImpersonationBanner.tsx       # (existing — add i18n)\n49: │   │   ├── ProtectedRoute.tsx            # (existing)\n50: │   │   ├── MarketingLayout.tsx           # NEW: public page wrapper\n51: │   │   ├── MarketingHeader.tsx           # NEW: public nav (Home, About, How It Works, Login, dark toggle, lang switcher)\n52: │   │   └── Footer.tsx                    # NEW: copyright, legal links, dark toggle, lang switcher\n53: │   ├── shared/\n54: │   │   ├── CookieBanner.tsx              # NEW: minimal consent notice\n55: │   │   ├── DarkModeToggle.tsx            # NEW: sun/moon icon button\n56: │   │   ├── LanguageSwitcher.tsx          # NEW: EN/PL toggle\n57: │   │   ├── EmptyState.tsx                # (existing — add i18n)\n58: │   │   ├── ErrorBoundary.tsx             # (existing)\n59: │   │   ├── ErrorFallback.tsx             # (existing — add i18n)\n60: │   │   ├── Loader.tsx                    # (existing — add i18n)\n61: │   │   ├── NotFoundPage.tsx              # (existing — add i18n)\n62: │   │   └── RouteErrorFallback.tsx        # (existing — add i18n)\n63: │   └── ui/\n64: │       ├── Badge.tsx                     # (existing)\n65: │       ├── Button.tsx                    # (existing)\n66: │       ├── Card.tsx                      # (existing)\n67: │       ├── Input.tsx                     # (existing — add i18n props)\n68: │       ├── Skeleton.tsx                  # (existing)\n69: │       ├── Spinner.tsx                   # (existing)\n70: │       ├── Toast.tsx                     # (existing — add i18n)\n71: │       └── ToastProvider.tsx             # (existing)\n72: ├── features/\n73: │   ├── marketing/\n74: │   │   ├── pages/\n75: │   │   │   ├── LandingPage.tsx           # NEW: hero + features + CTA\n76: │   │   │   ├── AboutPage.tsx             # NEW: project story + tech stack\n77: │   │   │   ├── HowItWorksPage.tsx        # NEW: step-by-step triage flow\n78: │   │   │   ├── PrivacyPage.tsx           # NEW: GDPR privacy policy\n79: │   │   │   ├── TermsPage.tsx             # NEW: demo disclaimer\n80: │   │   │   ├── CookiesPage.tsx           # NEW: what localStorage we use\n81: │   │   │   └── ContactPage.tsx           # NEW: link to portfolio\n82: │   │   └── components/\n83: │   │   ├── HeroSection.tsx           # NEW: landing hero with glassmorphism frosted card\n84: │   │   ├── StepCard.tsx              # NEW: How It Works step cards with timeline\n85: │   │   ├── TableOfContents.tsx       # NEW: sticky sidebar nav for legal pages\n86: │   │   └── DemoPreview.tsx           # NEW: screenshot browser-mockup section\n87: │   ├── auth/pages/                       # (existing — wrap with i18n)\n88: │   │   ├── LoginPage.tsx\n89: │   │   ├── RegisterPage.tsx\n90: │   │   └── VerifyEmailPage.tsx\n91: │   ├── triage/pages/                     # (existing — wrap with i18n)\n92: │   │   ├── TriagePage.tsx\n93: │   │   └── TriageResultPage.tsx\n94: │   ├── triage/components/                # (existing — wrap with i18n)\n95: │   │   ├── AnswerInput.tsx\n96: │   │   ├── ConversationBubble.tsx\n97: │   │   ├── OutcomeCard.tsx\n98: │   │   ├── SymptomInput.tsx\n99: │   │   └── UrgencyBadge.tsx\n100: │   ├── submissions/pages/                # (existing — wrap with i18n)\n101: │   │   └── MySubmissionsPage.tsx\n102: │   ├── submissions/components/           # (existing — wrap with i18n)\n103: │   │   └── SubmissionsList.tsx\n104: │   └── admin/pages/                      # (existing — wrap with i18n)\n105: │       ├── DashboardPage.tsx\n106: │       ├── SubmissionDetailPage.tsx\n107: │       └── UsersPage.tsx\n108: ├── styles/\n109: │   └── index.css                         # (expand — teal, slate, typography tokens)\n110: ├── routes.tsx                            # (add public routes, wrap in providers)\n111: ├── App.tsx                               # (add HelmetProvider, I18nProvider, ThemeProvider)\n112: ├── main.tsx                              # (existing)\n113: └── index.html                            # (update <title>, add lang attribute as template)\n114: ```\n115: \n116: ---\n117: \n118: ## Task 1: Install Dependencies + Expand Design Tokens\n119: \n120: **Files:**\n121: - Modify: `frontend/package.json`\n122: - Modify: `frontend/src/styles/index.css`\n123: \n124: - [ ] **Step 1: Install i18n + helmet + icon packages**\n125: \n126: ```bash\n127: cd frontend && pnpm add react-i18next i18next i18next-browser-languagedetector react-helmet-async lucide-react\n128: ```\n129: \n130: Expected: packages added to `package.json` and `node_modules/`.\n131: \n132: - [ ] **Step 2: Expand design tokens in index.css**\n133: \n134: Read current `frontend/src/styles/index.css`, then replace the `@theme` block with expanded tokens:\n135: \n136: ```css\n137: @import \"tailwindcss\";\n138: @import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Poppins:wght@600;700&display=swap');\n139: \n140: @variant dark (&:where(.dark, .dark *));\n141: \n142: @theme {\n143:   /* Primary — trust, clinical authority */\n144:   --color-primary-50: #eff6ff;\n145:   --color-primary-100: #dbeafe;\n146:   --color-primary-200: #bfdbfe;\n147:   --color-primary-300: #93c5fd;\n148:   --color-primary-400: #60a5fa;\n149:   --color-primary-500: #3b82f6;\n150:   --color-primary-600: #2563eb;\n151:   --color-primary-700: #1d4ed8;\n152:   --color-primary-800: #1e40af;\n153:   --color-primary-900: #1e3a5f;\n154:   --color-primary-950: #172554;\n155: \n156:   /* Accent — modern medical tech, teal */\n157:   --color-accent-50: #f0fdfa;\n158:   --color-accent-100: #ccfbf1;\n159:   --color-accent-200: #99f6e4;\n160:   --color-accent-300: #5eead4;\n161:   --color-accent-400: #2dd4bf;\n162:   --color-accent-500: #14b8a6;\n163:   --color-accent-600: #0d9488;\n164:   --color-accent-700: #0f766e;\n165:   --color-accent-800: #115e59;\n166:   --color-accent-900: #134e4a;\n167:   --color-accent-950: #042f2e;\n168: \n169:   /* Urgency scale — triage coding */\n170:   --color-urgency-low: #22c55e;\n171:   --color-urgency-medium: #eab308;\n172:   --color-urgency-high: #f97316;\n173:   --color-urgency-emergency: #ef4444;\n174: \n175:   /* Surface — clean clinical backgrounds */\n176:   --color-surface-50: #f8fafc;\n177:   --color-surface-100: #f1f5f9;\n178:   --color-surface-200: #e2e8f0;\n179:   --color-surface-300: #cbd5e1;\n180:   --color-surface-400: #94a3b8;\n181:   --color-surface-500: #64748b;\n182:   --color-surface-600: #475569;\n183:   --color-surface-700: #334155;\n184:   --color-surface-800: #1e293b;\n185:   --color-surface-900: #0f172a;\n186:   --color-surface-950: #020617;\n187: \n188:   /* Typography */\n189:   --font-sans: 'Inter', ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;\n190:   --font-heading: 'Poppins', 'Inter', ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;\n191:   --font-mono: 'JetBrains Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;\n192: \n193:   /* Radius */\n194:   --radius-sm: 0.375rem;\n195:   --radius-md: 0.5rem;\n196:   --radius-lg: 0.75rem;\n197:   --radius-xl: 1rem;\n198:   --radius-2xl: 1.5rem;\n199: }\n200: \n201: html {\n202:   @apply bg-white text-gray-900 dark:bg-gray-950 dark:text-gray-100;\n203: }\n204: \n205: body {\n206:   @apply antialiased;\n207: }\n208: ```\n209: \n210: - [ ] **Step 3: Verify build still passes**\n211: \n212: ```bash\n213: cd frontend && pnpm build\n214: ```\n215: \n216: Expected: build succeeds (0 errors). New tokens available via `bg-accent-500`, `text-surface-700`, etc.\n217: \n218: - [ ] **Step 4: Commit**\n219: \n220: ```bash\n221: cd frontend && git add package.json pnpm-lock.yaml src/styles/index.css\n222: git commit -m \"feat: install i18n/helmet/lucide deps, add Poppins font, expand design tokens with teal accent, surface scale, typography, and radius tokens\"\n223: ```\n224: \n225: ---\n226: \n227: ## Task 2: i18n Infrastructure — Setup + EN Locale Files\n228: \n229: **Files:**\n230: - Create: `frontend/src/i18n/index.ts`\n231: - Create: `frontend/src/i18n/locales/en/common.json`\n232: - Create: `frontend/src/i18n/locales/en/landing.json`\n233: - Create: `frontend/src/i18n/locales/en/about.json`\n234: - Create: `frontend/src/i18n/locales/en/howItWorks.json`\n235: - Create: `frontend/src/i18n/locales/en/legal.json`\n236: - Create: `frontend/src/i18n/locales/en/auth.json`\n237: - Create: `frontend/src/i18n/locales/en/triage.json`\n238: - Create: `frontend/src/i18n/locales/en/admin.json`\n239: \n240: - [ ] **Step 1: Create i18n initialization**\n241: \n242: `frontend/src/i18n/index.ts`:\n243: \n244: ```typescript\n245: import i18n from 'i18next';\n246: import { initReactI18next } from 'react-i18next';\n247: import LanguageDetector from 'i18next-browser-languagedetector';\n248: \n249: import common from './locales/en/common.json';\n250: import landing from './locales/en/landing.json';\n251: import about from './locales/en/about.json';\n252: import howItWorks from './locales/en/howItWorks.json';\n253: import legal from './locales/en/legal.json';\n254: import auth from './locales/en/auth.json';\n255: import triage from './locales/en/triage.json';\n256: import admin from './locales/en/admin.json';\n257: \n258: i18n\n259:   .use(LanguageDetector)\n260:   .use(initReactI18next)\n261:   .init({\n262:     resources: {\n263:       en: {\n264:         common,\n265:         landing,\n266:         about,\n267:         howItWorks,\n268:         legal,\n269:         auth,\n270:         triage,\n271:         admin,\n272:       },\n273:     },\n274:     fallbackLng: 'en',\n275:     defaultNS: 'common',\n276:     interpolation: {\n277:       escapeValue: false, // React already escapes\n278:     },\n279:     detection: {\n280:       order: ['localStorage', 'navigator'],\n281:       caches: ['localStorage'],\n282:       lookupLocalStorage: 'i18nextLng',\n283:     },\n284:   });\n285: \n286: export default i18n;\n287: ```\n288: \n289: - [ ] **Step 2: Create English locale files**\n290: \n291: `frontend/src/i18n/locales/en/common.json`:\n292: \n293: ```json\n294: {\n295:   \"appName\": \"TriageFlow\",\n296:   \"tagline\": \"AI-Powered Patient Pre-Screening Demo\",\n297:   \"nav\": {\n298:     \"home\": \"Home\",\n299:     \"about\": \"About\",\n300:     \"howItWorks\": \"How It Works\",\n301:     \"login\": \"Log In\",\n302:     \"register\": \"Register\",\n303:     \"logout\": \"Log Out\",\n304:     \"newTriage\": \"New Triage\",\n305:     \"mySubmissions\": \"My Submissions\",\n306:     \"admin\": \"Admin\",\n307:     \"backToAdmin\": \"Back to Admin\"\n308:   },\n309:   \"footer\": {\n310:     \"copyright\": \"© 2026 Piotr Świderski. All rights reserved.\",\n311:     \"builtWith\": \"Built with Symfony, React, and AI — a portfolio project.\",\n312:     \"privacy\": \"Privacy Policy\",\n313:     \"terms\": \"Terms of Service\",\n314:     \"cookies\": \"Cookie Policy\",\n315:     \"contact\": \"Contact\"\n316:   },\n317:   \"languageSwitcher\": {\n318:     \"label\": \"Language\",\n319:     \"en\": \"English\",\n320:     \"pl\": \"Polski\"\n321:   },\n322:   \"darkMode\": {\n323:     \"toggle\": \"Toggle dark mode\",\n324:     \"light\": \"Light mode\",\n325:     \"dark\": \"Dark mode\"\n326:   },\n327:   \"cookieBanner\": {\n328:     \"message\": \"This demo uses browser storage for authentication and preferences. No tracking. No cookies (in the traditional sense).\",\n329:     \"accept\": \"OK, got it\"\n330:   },\n331:   \"loading\": \"Loading...\",\n332:   \"error\": {\n333:     \"title\": \"Something went wrong\",\n334:     \"retry\": \"Try Again\",\n335:     \"goHome\": \"Go Home\",\n336:     \"details\": \"Error details\"\n337:   },\n338:   \"notFound\": {\n339:     \"title\": \"Page Not Found\",\n340:     \"message\": \"The page you're looking for doesn't exist.\",\n341:     \"goHome\": \"Go to Home\"\n342:   },\n343:   \"empty\": {\n344:     \"title\": \"Nothing here yet\",\n345:     \"message\": \"Check back later.\"\n346:   }\n347: }\n348: ```\n349: \n350: `frontend/src/i18n/locales/en/landing.json`:\n351: \n352: ```json\n353: {\n354:   \"hero\": {\n355:     \"title\": \"Tired of waiting for your first-contact medical specialist?\",\n356:     \"subtitle\": \"Let's hallucinate who can help you based on your symptoms!\",\n357:     \"disclaimer\": \"In case of a real medical issue, please contact a human specialist. This is a demonstration system.\",\n358:     \"cta\": \"Try the Demo\",\n359:     \"secondaryCta\": \"See How It Works\"\n360:   },\n361:   \"features\": {\n362:     \"title\": \"What This Demo Showcases\",\n363:     \"aiTriage\": {\n364:       \"title\": \"AI-Powered Triage\",\n365:       \"description\": \"An LLM-driven interview pipeline that asks follow-up questions and produces a triage recommendation — specialist, urgency, and justification.\"\n366:     },\n367:     \"fullStack\": {\n368:       \"title\": \"Full-Stack Architecture\",\n369:       \"description\": \"Symfony 7.4 backend with DDD-inspired bounded contexts, async message queue, and PostgreSQL. React 19 frontend with TypeScript and TanStack Query.\"\n370:     },\n371:     \"synthetic\": {\n372:       \"title\": \"Synthetic Case Generator\",\n373:       \"description\": \"A cron-driven scheduler that generates realistic symptom descriptions and simulates patient-AI conversations — the system runs itself.\"\n374:     },\n375:     \"observability\": {\n376:       \"title\": \"Observability & Monitoring\",\n377:       \"description\": \"Structured logging with correlation IDs, failed message recovery, CI pipeline with PHPStan level 5.\"\n378:     }\n379:   },\n380:   \"techStack\": {\n381:     \"title\": \"Tech Stack\",\n382:     \"backend\": \"Backend\",\n383:     \"frontend\": \"Frontend\",\n384:     \"infra\": \"Infrastructure\"\n385:   }\n386: }\n387: ```\n388: \n389: `frontend/src/i18n/locales/en/about.json`:\n390: \n391: ```json\n392: {\n393:   \"title\": \"About This Project\",\n394:   \"intro\": \"TriageFlow is a two-week portfolio project demonstrating full-stack development proficiency with modern tools and AI integration.\",\n395:   \"who\": {\n396:     \"title\": \"Who Built This\",\n397:     \"description\": \"Built by Piotr Świderski — a full-stack developer exploring the intersection of AI, healthcare simulation, and modern web architecture.\"\n398:   },\n399:   \"why\": {\n400:     \"title\": \"Why TriageFlow\",\n401:     \"description\": \"The medical triage domain provides rich modeling challenges: state machines, async messaging, AI pipelines, and role-based access control — all in a compact, demonstrable scope.\"\n402:   },\n403:   \"disclaimer\": {\n404:     \"title\": \"Important Disclaimer\",\n405:     \"description\": \"TriageFlow is a demonstration system. It does not provide real medical advice. All triage recommendations are generated by AI for illustrative purposes only. If you have a medical concern, please consult a qualified healthcare professional.\"\n406:   }\n407: }\n408: ```\n409: \n410: `frontend/src/i18n/locales/en/howItWorks.json`:\n411: \n412: ```json\n413: {\n414:   \"title\": \"How It Works\",\n415:   \"subtitle\": \"A 4-step AI-powered triage pipeline, from symptom to recommendation.\",\n416:   \"steps\": {\n417:     \"step1\": {\n418:       \"title\": \"1. Describe Your Symptoms\",\n419:       \"description\": \"You start by describing what's bothering you — in your own words, just like you would to a real doctor. No forms, no checkboxes.\"\n420:     },\n421:     \"step2\": {\n422:       \"title\": \"2. AI Follow-Up Questions\",\n423:       \"description\": \"The AI analyzes your description and asks clarifying follow-up questions, just like a triage nurse would. Up to 3 rounds of Q&A.\"\n424:     },\n425:     \"step3\": {\n426:       \"title\": \"3. Triage Recommendation\",\n427:       \"description\": \"When the AI has enough information, it produces a recommendation: which specialist you should see, how urgent it is, and why.\"\n428:     },\n429:     \"step4\": {\n430:       \"title\": \"4. Review & Next Steps\",\n431:       \"description\": \"You can review your full conversation history and the triage outcome. The system is transparent — you see exactly what the AI saw.\"\n432:     }\n433:   },\n434:   \"cta\": \"Try It Yourself\",\n435:   \"disclaimer\": \"Remember: this is a demo. Not real medical advice. See our Terms of Service for details.\"\n436: }\n437: ```\n438: \n439: `frontend/src/i18n/locales/en/legal.json`:\n440: \n441: ```json\n442: {\n443:   \"privacy\": {\n444:     \"title\": \"Privacy Policy\",\n445:     \"lastUpdated\": \"Last updated: June 13, 2026\",\n446:     \"intro\": \"TriageFlow is a demonstration portfolio project. This privacy policy explains what data we collect and how we use it.\",\n447:     \"dataCollected\": {\n448:       \"title\": \"What Data We Collect\",\n449:       \"items\": [\n450:         \"Email address — used for account registration and login.\",\n451:         \"Symptom descriptions — the text you enter during triage interviews.\",\n452:         \"Triage outcomes — AI-generated recommendations based on your symptoms.\"\n453:       ]\n454:     },\n455:     \"dataUsage\": {\n456:       \"title\": \"How We Use Your Data\",\n457:       \"items\": [\n458:         \"Authentication: your email identifies your account.\",\n459:         \"Triage functionality: your symptom descriptions are sent to an AI model (OpenRouter) to generate triage recommendations.\",\n460:         \"No data is sold, shared with third parties, or used for marketing.\"\n461:       ]\n462:     },\n463:     \"storage\": {\n464:       \"title\": \"Data Storage\",\n465:       \"items\": [\n466:         \"All data is stored in a PostgreSQL database.\",\n467:         \"JWT authentication tokens are stored in your browser's localStorage.\",\n468:         \"Language and theme preferences are stored in localStorage.\",\n469:         \"No tracking cookies, analytics, or third-party scripts are used.\"\n470:       ]\n471:     },\n472:     \"rights\": {\n473:       \"title\": \"Your Rights\",\n474:       \"description\": \"As this is a demo system with no persistent production deployment, data may be reset at any time. You can delete your account and all associated data by contacting the developer.\"\n475:     },\n476:     \"contact\": \"For privacy-related questions, contact piotr@piotrswiderski.dev\"\n477:   },\n478:   \"terms\": {\n479:     \"title\": \"Terms of Service\",\n480:     \"lastUpdated\": \"Last updated: June 13, 2026\",\n481:     \"intro\": \"By using TriageFlow, you acknowledge and agree to the following terms.\",\n482:     \"demoNature\": {\n483:       \"title\": \"Demonstration System\",\n484:       \"description\": \"TriageFlow is a portfolio demonstration project, not a production medical service. All triage recommendations are generated by artificial intelligence for illustrative purposes only.\"\n485:     },\n486:     \"notMedicalAdvice\": {\n487:       \"title\": \"Not Medical Advice\",\n488:       \"description\": \"The AI-generated triage recommendations are not real medical advice. They are synthetic demonstrations of what an AI triage pipeline could produce. Do not rely on them for actual medical decisions. If you have a medical concern, consult a qualified healthcare professional immediately.\"\n489:     },\n490:     \"noLiability\": {\n491:       \"title\": \"No Liability\",\n492:       \"description\": \"The developer assumes no liability for any actions taken based on the AI-generated content in this demo application. Use is entirely at your own risk.\"\n493:     },\n494:     \"dataHandling\": {\n495:       \"title\": \"Data Handling\",\n496:       \"description\": \"Data submitted to this demo may be processed by third-party AI providers (OpenRouter). No data is sold or used for purposes beyond the demo functionality. See our Privacy Policy for details.\"\n497:     }\n498:   },\n499:   \"cookies\": {\n500:     \"title\": \"Cookie Policy\",\n501:     \"lastUpdated\": \"Last updated: June 13, 2026\",\n502:     \"intro\": \"TriageFlow doesn't use traditional browser cookies. Here's what we store in your browser:\",\n503:     \"localStorage\": {\n504:       \"title\": \"Local Storage Usage\",\n505:       \"items\": [\n506:         \"JWT authentication token — required to keep you logged in (essential).\",\n507:         \"Language preference — remembers whether you chose English or Polish (preference).\",\n508:         \"Theme preference — remembers whether you chose light or dark mode (preference).\",\n509:         \"Cookie consent acknowledgment — remembers that you've seen the consent notice.\"\n510:       ]\n511:     },\n512:     \"sessionStorage\": {\n513:       \"title\": \"Session Storage Usage\",\n514:       \"items\": [\n515:         \"Admin impersonation state — temporarily stores the admin's original token during user impersonation. Cleared when the tab is closed.\"\n516:       ]\n517:     },\n518:     \"noTracking\": {\n519:       \"title\": \"No Tracking\",\n520:       \"description\": \"We do not use any analytics, tracking cookies, third-party scripts, or any form of user behavior tracking. This is a demo application — what you see is what you get.\"\n521:     }\n522:   }\n523: }\n524: ```\n525: \n526: `frontend/src/i18n/locales/en/auth.json`:\n527: \n528: ```json\n529: {\n530:   \"login\": {\n531:     \"title\": \"Log In\",\n532:     \"email\": \"Email\",\n533:     \"emailPlaceholder\": \"you@example.com\",\n534:     \"password\": \"Password\",\n535:     \"passwordPlaceholder\": \"Enter your password\",\n536:     \"submit\": \"Log In\",\n537:     \"submitting\": \"Logging in...\",\n538:     \"noAccount\": \"Don't have an account?\",\n539:     \"registerLink\": \"Register\",\n540:     \"invalidCredentials\": \"Invalid email or password.\",\n541:     \"unverified\": \"Please verify your email address before logging in.\",\n542:     \"registrationSuccess\": \"Account created! Check your email to verify your address, then log in.\",\n543:     \"checkMailpit\": \"In development: check Mailpit at http://localhost:8025 for the verification email.\"\n544:   },\n545:   \"register\": {\n546:     \"title\": \"Create Account\",\n547:     \"email\": \"Email\",\n548:     \"emailPlaceholder\": \"you@example.com\",\n549:     \"password\": \"Password\",\n550:     \"passwordPlaceholder\": \"Min. 8 characters\",\n551:     \"confirmPassword\": \"Confirm Password\",\n552:     \"confirmPasswordPlaceholder\": \"Repeat your password\",\n553:     \"submit\": \"Create Account\",\n554:     \"submitting\": \"Creating account...\",\n555:     \"haveAccount\": \"Already have an account?\",\n556:     \"loginLink\": \"Log In\",\n557:     \"passwordMismatch\": \"Passwords do not match.\",\n558:     \"emailTaken\": \"This email is already registered.\",\n559:     \"validation\": {\n560:       \"emailRequired\": \"Email is required.\",\n561:       \"emailInvalid\": \"Please enter a valid email.\",\n562:       \"passwordRequired\": \"Password is required.\",\n563:       \"pa