              "description": "Task 10: Provider wiring",
              "prompt": "You are implementing Task 10 of the Business Website Layer plan: Provider wiring in main.tsx and App.tsx.\n\n## Dependencies (already installed)\n- react-helmet-async (HelmetProvider)\n- react-i18next (already configured in src/i18n/index.ts)\n- All locale files exist at src/i18n/locales/{en,pl}/*.json\n\n## What to do\n\n### Step 1: Read existing files\nRead the current `frontend/src/main.tsx` and `frontend/src/App.tsx` to understand the existing structure.\n\n### Step 2: Modify main.tsx\nAdd HelmetProvider wrapping and ensure i18n is imported before App mounts. The file should look like:\n\n```tsx\nimport React from 'react';\nimport ReactDOM from 'react-dom/client';\nimport { QueryClient, QueryClientProvider } from '@tanstack/react-query';\nimport { HelmetProvider } from 'react-helmet-async';\nimport { ToastProvider } from './components/ui/ToastProvider';\nimport './i18n';\nimport './styles/index.css';\n\nconst queryClient = new QueryClient({\n  defaultOptions: {\n    queries: {\n      staleTime: 30_000,\n      refetchOnWindowFocus: false,\n    },\n  },\n});\n\nReactDOM.createRoot(document.getElementById('root')!).render(\n  <React.StrictMode>\n    <HelmetProvider>\n      <QueryClientProvider client={queryClient}>\n        <ToastProvider />\n      </QueryClientProvider>\n    </HelmetProvider>\n  </React.StrictMode>,\n);\n```\n\n### Step 3: Modify App.tsx\nAdd ThemeInit component that applies dark mode on mount (from localStorage or system preference). The file should look like:\n\n```tsx\nimport { lazy, Suspense } from 'react'\nimport { RouterProvider } from 'react-router-dom'\nimport { AuthProvider } from './components/auth/AuthProvider'\nimport { Loader } from './components/shared/Loader'\nimport { router } from './routes'\n\nconst AdminDashboardPage = lazy(() => import('./features/admin/pages/DashboardPage'))\nconst AdminSubmissionDetailPage = lazy(() => import('./features/admin/pages/SubmissionDetailPage'))\n\nfunction ThemeInit() {\n  // This runs synchronously before first render\n  const stored = localStorage.getItem('theme')\n    const prefersDark = window.matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').matches\n    if (stored === 'dark' || (!stored && prefersDark)) {\n      document.documentElement.classList.add('dark')\n    } else {\n      document.documentElement.classList.remove('dark')\n    }\n  return null\n}\n\nexport default function App() {\n  return (\n    <>\n      <ThemeInit />\n      <AuthProvider>\n        <RouterProvider router={router} fallbackElement={\n          <Suspense fallback={<Loader message=\"Loading...\" />}>\n            <AdminDashboardPage />\n            <AdminSubmissionDetailPage />\n          </Suspense>\n        } />\n      </AuthProvider>\n    </>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nCRITICAL: Match the existing import structure and patterns from the current App.tsx. Preserve any existing lazy imports, Suspense patterns, and the AuthProvider structure. Read the current file first and adapt — don't just overwrite blindly.\n\n### Step 4: Verify\nAfter writing both files, verify the imports resolve correctly by reading them back. Check that:\n- HelmetProvider is imported and wraps the tree in main.tsx\n- ThemeInit runs before AuthProvider renders\n- All existing lazy imports are preserved\n- i18n is imported before anything else\n\nReturn a completion report with: files modified, any deviations from the plan, and verification status.",
