use**: `getByText` matches any element containing the feature title text (heading + possibly description excerpts). Heading role eliminates false matches.\n- **Fix**: Targets only `<h3>` elements (feature card titles), avoiding ambiguity with description paragraphs.\n\n### Fix 5: PrivacyPage.test.tsx — \"renders page title\" (line 18)\n| Before | After |\n|--------|-------|\n| `screen.getByText(/Privacy Policy/i)` | `screen.getByRole('heading', { name: /Privacy Policy/i, level: 1 })` |\n\n- **Root cause**: `\"Privacy Policy\"` could match the `<h1>` AND Helmet-rendered title text in the DOM body (react-helmet-async behavior without a `HelmetProvider` wrapper in tests).\n- **Fix**: Heading role + level 1 targets only the `<h1>`, avoiding any Helmet-leaked text.\n\n---\n\n### Files Modified\n- `frontend/src/test/marketing/AboutPage.test.tsx` — lines 18, 33\n- `frontend/src/test/marketing/LandingPage.test.tsx` — lines 32, 44\n- `frontend/src/test/marketing/PrivacyPage.test.tsx` — line 18\n\n### Self-Review: ✅ Types clean | ✅ Imports verified | ✅ No debug artifacts | ✅ All acceptance criteria met | ✅ External libs verified\n</task_result>\n</task>",
