          "text": "## ✅ Business Website Layer — Complete\n\nAll 17 tasks executed across 8 parallel batches. Here's the final state:\n\n### Verification (all clean)\n\n| Check | Status |\n|-------|--------|\n| TypeScript (`tsc --noEmit`) | ✅ 0 errors |\n| ESLint (`eslint src/`) | ✅ 0 errors, 0 warnings |\n| Vitest tests | ✅ **136/136 pass** (21 test files) |\n| Vite build | ✅ 226 modules, 243ms |\n\n### What Was Built\n\n**Public website (7 new pages):**\n| Page | Route | Key Design |\n|------|-------|-----------|\n| Landing | `/` | Glassmorphism hero, 4 feature cards (Lucide icons), demo preview, tech stack grid |\n| About | `/about` | Developer identity, Tech Decisions grid, amber disclaimer |\n| How It Works | `/how-it-works` | Vertical timeline with gradient number circles |\n| Privacy | `/privacy` | Sticky ToC sidebar, 6 card-wrapped sections |\n| Terms | `/terms` | Section-specific icons (FlaskConical/Stethoscope/ShieldOff/Database) |\n| Cookies | `/cookies` | Storage/tracking sections with icons, ToC |\n| Contact | `/contact` | Frosted card, 2×2 social grid (Portfolio/GitHub/LinkedIn/Email) |\n\n**Shared infrastructure:**\n- **i18n**: EN + PL across 16 JSON locale files, all 26 source components migrated\n- **Dark mode**: `useDarkMode` hook (system pref + localStorage), toggle button everywhere\n- **Cookie consent**: Minimal one-click banner with localStorage persistence\n- **Language switcher**: Segmented EN|PL control in header + footer\n- **MarketingLayout**: Sticky header (mobile hamburger drawer) + 3-column footer\n- **Lucide icons**: Tree-shakeable SVG icons replacing emojis\n- **Poppins font**: Heading font for marketing pages (600/700 weights)\n- **Design tokens**: Full primary/accent/surface scales, radius/font tokens\n\n**Backend:** RegistrationController sends localized email (PL via `Accept-Language` header)\n\n### Files Changed\n\n~65 files created/modified across frontend, 1 file modified in backend.\n\n### Next Steps\n\n1. **Start the app** (`cd frontend && npm run dev`, `cd backend && symfony serve -d`) and verify visually\n2. **Commit & push** — both repos\n3. **Update Issue #11** on GitHub with completion summary\n4. The **accessibility audit** (original Issue #11 Phase 2 HITL) can proceed as a follow-up — the app is now accessible-by-default (focus rings, ARIA labels, semantic HTML) but a manual audit is still recommended per the handoff checklist",
