            "output": "<task id=\"ses_139ceef7dffepvdxNXsZpouTqx\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\nNow I have a complete picture. Let me compile the review.\n\n---\n\n# Code Review: Business Website Layer\n\n**Reviewing... what would you devs do if I didn't check up on you?**\n\nReviewed scope: ~40 files across frontend (React/TypeScript/i18n/Tailwind) and 1 backend file (PHP/Symfony). Plan coverage: Tasks 1–17 against `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-13-business-website-layer.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Strengths\n\n- **Complete i18n coverage**: All 16 locale files (8 EN + 8 PL) are present with consistent key structures across languages. The EN↔PL parity is thorough — every string is translated.\n- **Dark mode implementation is correct**: `useDarkMode` hook follows the right pattern — system preference detection, localStorage persistence, media query listener for real-time OS changes, and the `ThemeInit` bootstrap handles the flash-of-wrong-theme problem (modulo the render-side-effect issue noted below).\n- **Route restructuring is well-organized**: The dual-layout approach (AppLayout vs MarketingLayout) with AppLayout routes declared first so specific paths beat the MarketingLayout catch-all is a clever ordering trick that works correctly.\n- **Design token expansion is comprehensive**: Primary, accent, surface, urgency, typography, and radius tokens — all correctly wired into Tailwind v4 `@theme`. Poppins font import, dark variant setup — all solid.\n- **TableOfContents with IntersectionObserver**: Clean implementation with active section highlighting, proper cleanup on unmount.\n- **Backend `RegistrationController` change is well-scoped**: Minimal, focused, uses Symfony's built-in `getPreferredLanguage()`, wraps email sending in try/catch (correct for dev/demo).\n- **All verification gates pass**: 136/136 tests, TSC clean, ESLint clean, build succeeds.\n\n---\n\n## Issues\n\n### Critical (Must Fix)\n\n#### C1: `ThemeInit` runs side effects during render — React anti-pattern\n**File:** `frontend/src/App.tsx:6-15`\n**What's wrong:** `ThemeInit` directly manipulates `document.documentElement.classList` and reads `localStorage` during React's render phase — not inside `useEffect`. This violates the Rules of React: [render must be a pure function](https://react.dev/reference/rules/components-must-be-pure).\n**Why it matters:** Causes the dark mode class to be applied synchronously before React hydrates, which is actually fine for the FOUC-prevention case — but `localStorage.getItem()` is a side effect that belongs in `useEffect`. The component also returns `null` unconditionally, which works by accident because React batches the DOM mutation before the return.\n**How to fix:** The pattern is correct as a pre-React bootstrap — but should be in `main.tsx` (before `createRoot().render()`) rather than inside a component:\n```tsx\n// In main.tsx, BEFORE createRoot().render():\nconst stored = localStorage.getItem('theme');\nif (stored === 'dark' || (!stored && window.matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').matches)) {\n  document.documentElement.classList.add('dark');\n}\n// Then remove ThemeInit from App.tsx entirely.\n```\nThis is the standard pattern (see: Tailwind CSS dark mode docs, next-themes).\n\n#### C2: `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` used for plain text content (XSS risk if content ever becomes dynamic)\n**File:** `frontend/src/features/marketing/pages/AboutPage.tsx:34-35, 57-58, 66-67`\n**What's wrong:** `t('intro')`, `t('who.body')`, and `t('why.body')` return plain text strings (no HTML tags), but are rendered via `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`. Only `t('disclaimer.body')` contains HTML.\n**Why it matters:** If these translation strings were ever moved to a CMS or user-editable source, this becomes a direct XSS vector. Even for static content, it sets a dangerous precedent.\n**How to fix:** Render plain text keys as regular React text nodes:\n```tsx\n// For intro, who.body, why.body — use regular text:\n<p className=\"...\">{t('intro')}</p>\n\n// Only disclaimer.body needs dangerouslySetInnerHTML since it uses <p>, <strong>, class attributes\n```\n\n---\n\n### Important (Should Fix)\n\n#### I1: Route architecture places login/register under AppLayout — shows authenticated header to unauthenticated users\n**File:** `frontend/src/routes.tsx:31-92`\n**What's wrong:** Login and Register pages are children of `AppLayout`, which renders the authenticated `Header` component (with navigation for triage, submissions, admin, logout). Unauthenticated users at `/login` will see an app shell that implies they're logged in.\n**Plan says:** Unauth pages should be in their own group: \"Unauth Pages (no layout wrapper — use their own design)\" (plan line 2791). And the MarketingLayout was supposed to wrap the public surface.\n**Why it matters:** Confusing UX. A first-time visitor at `/login` sees navigation elements (My Submissions, New Triage, Admin) that are irrelevant and potentially confusing.\n**How to fix:** Extract login/register routes into their own route group (without AppLayout) or under MarketingLayout, as the plan specified:\n```tsx\n// Separate group for unauth pages (no AppLayout):\n{\n  errorElement: <RouteErrorFallback />,\n  children: [\n    { path: 'login', lazy: () => import('./features/auth/pages/LoginPage')... },\n    { path: 'register', lazy: () => import('./features/auth/pages/RegisterPage')... },\n    { path: 'verify-email', element: <VerifyEmailPage /> },\n  ],\n},\n```\n\n#### I2: `TableOfContents` has hardcoded English string — not i18n-aware\n**File:** `frontend/src/features/marketing/components/TableOfContents.tsx:39`\n**What's wrong:** `\"On this page\"` is hardcoded in English. When viewing Privacy/Terms/Cookies pages in Polish, all content is translated except this sidebar label.\n**How to fix:**\n```tsx\nimport { useTranslation } from 'react-i18next';\n// ...\nconst { t } = useTranslation('legal');\n// ...\n<p className=\"...\">{t('toc.label')}</p>\n// Add \"toc\": { \"label\": \"On this page\" } to EN legal.json\n// Add \"toc\": { \"label\": \"Na tej stronie\" } to PL legal.json\n```\n\n#### I3: Unnecessary `useEffect`/`useState` in `CookieBanner` — simpler with lazy initializer but misses plan's pattern\n**File:** `frontend/src/components/shared/CookieBanner.tsx:6`\n**Current code:** Uses `useState(() => !localStorage.getItem('cookieConsent'))` — this is actually fine and an improvement over the plan's `useEffect`. However, the initial render still flashes the banner if consent was already given, because the lazy initializer runs synchronously.\n**Actually:** This is already correct — the lazy initializer reads localStorage synchronously during render, so `visible` is `false` immediately when consent exists. **No change needed.** Retracting this — but noting it as a positive deviation from the plan.\n\n#### I4: Landing page is missing the Features section title\n**File:** `frontend/src/features/marketing/pages/LandingPage.tsx:76-104`\n**What's wrong:** The locale file has `features.title` = \"What This Demo Showcases\" (EN) / \"Co Demonstruje Ten Projekt\" (PL), but it's never rendered. The features grid appears without a heading.\n**Plan says:** The plan's LandingPage included `<h2>{t('landing:features.title')}</h2>` before the features grid.\n**How to fix:** Add the heading back:\n```tsx\n<h2 className=\"text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-center font-heading mb-16\">\n  {t('features.title')}\n</h2>\n```\n\n#### I5: `ContactPage` LinkedIn URL differs from the plan\n**File:** `frontend/src/features/marketing/pages/ContactPage.tsx:59`\n**Issue:** Uses `linkedin.com/in/piotr-swiderski` but plan specifies `linkedin.com/in/psswid`. \n**Why it matters:** One of these is wrong. Broken social link = bad portfolio impression.\n\n#### I6: Backend localized email body omits signature\n**File:** `backend/src/User/Infrastructure/Controller/RegistrationController.php:92-105`\n**What's wrong:** The plan specified email bodies ending with `\\n\\n— TriageFlow`. The actual emails don't include this signature. Minor but inconsistent.\n**How to fix:** Add `\\n\\n— TriageFlow` (or `\\n\\n— TriageFlow` in PL) to both email bodies.\n\n#### I7: Mobile hamburger menu aria-label is hardcoded English\n**File:** `frontend/src/components/layout/MarketingHeader.tsx:68`\n**Issue:** `aria-label={menuOpen ? 'Close menu' : 'Open menu'}` — not translated.\n**How to fix:** Add to common.json locale:\n```json\n\"header\": { \"openMenu\": \"Open menu\", \"closeMenu\": \"Close menu\" }\n```\nAnd use `t('common:header.openMenu')` / `t('common:header.closeMenu')`.\n\n#### I8: Unused `hero.disclaimer` key in landing locale files\n**File:** `frontend/src/i18n/locales/en/landing.json:5`, same in PL\n**What's wrong:** `hero.disclaimer` exists but is never referenced by LandingPage. The plan's LandingPage rendered it under the hero subtitle. Dead code in locale files.\n**Action:** Either render it in the LandingPage hero section (between subtitle and CTAs as the plan intended) or remove the key.\n\n#### I9: `CookiesPage` renders `cookies.banner` twice — as both heading and body\n**File:** `frontend/src/features/marketing/pages/CookiesPage.tsx:54-61`\n**What's wrong:** Lines 56-59 show:\n```tsx\n<h2>{t('cookies.banner')}</h2>\n<p>{t('cookies.banner')}</p>\n```\nThe same translation string is used for both heading and paragraph text. This renders the full paragraph twice.\n**How to fix:** The last section should either use a different key or just be a single paragraph:\n```tsx\n<p className=\"text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 leading-relaxed\">\n  {t('cookies.banner')}\n</p>\n```\n\n#### I10: Test coverage for new features is minimal (9 tests for 17 tasks)\n**What's missing:** No tests for: CookieBanner, LanguageSwitcher, TermsPage, CookiesPage, ContactPage, HowItWorksPage, TableOfContents, DemoPreview, MarketingHeader, Footer, MarketingLayout, StepCard, backend RegistrationController i18n change.\n**Why it matters:** The project's TDD mandate (.opencode/config.json says `requireTdd: true`) and the 80% coverage target are not met for the new features.\n**Recommendation:** At minimum, add tests for:\n- `CookieBanner` (renders/hides based on localStorage)\n- `LanguageSwitcher` (switches language, updates aria-pressed)\n- `HowItWorksPage` (renders 4 step cards)\n- `backend RegistrationController` localized email test (mock `getPreferredLanguage`)\n\n---\n\n### Minor (Nice to Have)\n\n#### M1: Inconsistent quote/semicolon style across new files\nSome files use semicolons (`DarkModeToggle.tsx`, `routes.tsx`), others don't (`AboutPage.tsx`, `PrivacyPage.tsx`). The project's ESLint config doesn't enforce this, but it creates inconsistent style. Run `pnpm lint --fix` or add a Prettier config.\n\n#### M2: `DemoPreview` has browser chrome dots but no address bar\nThe 3-dot traffic lights (`bg-red-400`, `bg-yellow-400`, `bg-green-400`) are correct for macOS, but a browser mockup typically includes an address bar row. Not a bug, just less convincing as a mockup.\n\n#### M3: `GithubIcon` and `LinkedinIcon` are duplicated between `AboutPage` and `ContactPage`\nBoth files define identical inline SVG components. Extract to a shared component or use a library like `simple-icons`.\n\n#### M4: `lucide-react` `LinkedinIcon` is imported but the plan specifies using it\nThe plan uses `lucide-react`'s `LinkedinIcon` but ContactPage defines a custom SVG. lucide-react includes a LinkedIn icon. Either use it or remove the import note.\n\n#### M5: `refetchOnWindowFocus: false` in `main.tsx` deviates from plan\nThe plan specified `refetchOnWindowFocus: true`. The actual code has `false`. Since this is a demo app, `false` is actually better — but document why if it's intentional.\n\n#### M6: Landing page hero uses `max-w-3xl` while plan specified `max-w-2xl`\nTrivial, but means the glassmorphism card is wider than designed.\n\n#### M7: Tech stack categories differ from plan\nPlan had: Backend, Frontend, Infra, AI. Implementation has: Backend, Frontend, AI/ML, Infrastructure — with different items (e.g., \"TypeScript 6\" instead of \"TypeScript\", \"LLaMA 4\" and \"Gemma 4\" added, \"PHPStan L5\" moved to Infra from Backend).\n\n---\n\n## i18n Completeness Audit\n\n| Check | Status |\n|---|---|\n| All 16 locale files present (8 EN + 8 PL) | ✅ |\n| Key structure matches across EN↔PL | ✅ |\n| `HowItWorks` steps use numeric keys (consistent across languages) | ✅ |\n| `LandingPage` references `hero.secondary` (not `secondaryCta` as in plan) | ⚠️ plan deviation, internally consistent |\n| `hero.disclaimer` key exists but unused | ⚠️ dead key |\n| `features.title` exists but not rendered | ⚠️ missing rendering |\n| `TableOfContents` \"On this page\" hardcoded English | ❌ not i18n |\n| `MarketingHeader` mobile menu aria-label hardcoded English | ❌ not i18n |\n| All existing component i18n migrations complete (auth, triage, submissions, admin, shared) | ✅ (verified by TSC + test pass) |\n| Polish translations are idiomatic and complete | ✅ |\n\n---\n\n## Plan Deviation Summary\n\n| Deviation | Verdict |\n|---|---|\n| Routes: login/register under AppLayout instead of standalone | ❌ Problematic (UX confusion) |\n| Routes: AppLayout wraps all auth routes (not ProtectedRoute wrapping AppLayout) | ⚠️ Architectural shift — works but changes the layering |\n| Marketing pages use `export default` instead of named exports | ⚠️ Inconsistent with project standards |\n| `ThemeInit` as component instead of `main.tsx` bootstrap | ❌ React anti-pattern |\n| Landing page content restructured (missing features title, tech stack categories changed) | ⚠️ Acceptable creative choice |\n| `DemoPreview` uses inline SVG instead of external image placeholder | ✅ Improvement (offline-friendly) |\n| `CookieBanner` uses lazy initializer instead of `useEffect` | ✅ Improvement (no flash) |\n| `AboutPage` uses `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` for rich text sections | ⚠️ Proceed with caution (C2) |\n| Backend email text simpler than plan | ⚠️ Minor |\n| Contact page LinkedIn URL changed from `psswid` to `piotr-swiderski` | ❌ One of these is wrong |\n\n---\n\n## Assessment\n\n**Ready to merge?** **No — fix Critical items first.**\n\n**Reasoning:** Two critical React correctness issues (ThemeInit render side-effect, unnecessary dangerouslySetInnerHTML) and one important UX issue (login under AppLayout) should be resolved. The i18n holes (TableOfContents hardcoded string, mobile menu aria-label) and the double-rendered `cookies.banner` section are quick wins. Once C1, C2, I1, I2, I7, and I9 are addressed, this is merge-ready. The test gap (I10) is important for project standards but not blocking for a portfolio demo.\n</task_result>\n</task>",
