              "prompt": "Fix 4 code review issues in the TriageFlow frontend. All files are under `/home/stefan/dev/projects/triageflow/frontend/`.\n\n### C1: ThemeInit render side-effect (React anti-pattern)\n\n**Problem:** `App.tsx` has a `ThemeInit` component that reads `localStorage` and manipulates `document.documentElement.classList` during React's render phase — not inside `useEffect`.\n\n**Fix:** Move the dark mode initialization to `main.tsx`, BEFORE `createRoot().render()`. Remove ThemeInit from App.tsx entirely.\n\n**Read these files first:** `src/App.tsx`, `src/main.tsx`\n\n**In main.tsx**, add BEFORE the `createRoot(document.getElementById('root')!).render(...)` call:\n```tsx\n// Initialize dark mode before React hydrates to prevent flash\nconst stored = localStorage.getItem('theme');\nif (stored === 'dark' || stored === 'light') {\n  document.documentElement.classList.toggle('dark', stored === 'dark');\n} else if (window.matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').matches) {\n  document.documentElement.classList.add('dark');\n}\n```\n\n**In App.tsx**, remove the `ThemeInit` import and its JSX usage (`<ThemeInit />`). Keep everything else unchanged.\n\n---\n\n### I1: Login/register routes show authenticated Header to unauthenticated users\n\n**Problem:** Login and Register pages are children of `AppLayout` which renders the `Header` with navigation for \"New Triage\", \"My Submissions\", \"Admin\", \"Logout\". Unauthenticated visitors at `/login` see an app shell that implies they're logged in.\n\n**Fix:** Move login and register routes OUT of AppLayout into their own route group (no layout wrapper). Verify Email should stay with them. Read `src/routes.tsx` first.\n\nRestructure routes like this:\n```tsx\n{\n  // Group: Unauth pages (no AppLayout — standalone design)\n  errorElement: <RouteErrorFallback />,\n  children: [\n    { path: 'login', lazy: () => import('./features/auth/pages/LoginPage') },\n    { path: 'register', lazy: () => import('./features