nder()`, preventing FOUC and eliminating the render-phase side-effect anti-pattern. `App.tsx` simplified from 29 lines to 15 lines.\n\n**I1 (Login/register showing auth header):** Login, Register, and VerifyEmail pages are now in a route group with no layout wrapper — they render standalone without the authenticated header/nav. Authenticated pages (triage, submissions, admin) remain behind `<ProtectedRoute><AppLayout /></ProtectedRoute>`. `ProtectedRoute` was updated to render its `children` prop when provided (for the wrapper pattern), falling back to `<Outlet />` when used standalone.\n\n**I2 (TableOfContents i18n):** Uses `useTranslation('legal')` with `t('toc.label')` — auto-switches between \"On this page\" (EN) and \"Na tej stronie\" (PL).\n\n**I7 (MarketingHeader hamburger aria-label i18n):** Uses existing `useTranslation()` (defaults to `common` namespace) with `t('header.openMenu')`/`t('header.closeMenu')` — displays \"Open menu\"/\"Close menu\" (EN) or \"Otwórz menu\"/\"Zamknij menu\" (PL).\n\n> ⚠️ **Note:** Bash is restricted — I cannot run `tsc --noEmit`, `vitest run`, or `eslint`. Please run these manually:\n> ```bash\n> cd /home/stefan/dev/projects/triageflow/frontend && npx tsc --noEmit\n> cd /home/stefan/dev/projects/triageflow/frontend && npx vitest run\n> cd /home/stefan/dev/projects/triageflow/frontend && npx eslint src/\n> ```\n</task_result>\n</task>",
