          "text": "<path>/home/stefan/dev/projects/triageflow/raw_log.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # TriageFlow — Raw Log\n2: \n3: Personal notes, thoughts, and observations during development.\n4: \n5: ---\n6: \n7: ## 2026-05-26\n8: \n9: - **Workflow setup**: Installed Matt Pocock skills (grill-with-docs, handoff, to-issues, zoom-out, caveman), created task template + tools matrix\n10: - **Repo layout**: triageflow root = docs repo (OpenCode config + docs), backend/ and frontend/ are separate repos\n11: - **Next**: Start Phase 1 (Foundation) from agents.md\n12: \n13: ## 2026-05-28\n14: \n15: **Full pipeline session (ALIGN → PLAN → ISSUES).** Completed the three discovery stages for Phase 1 Foundation:\n16: \n17: - 🧠 **ALIGN** (`grill-with-docs`): Defined domain language — Triage Submission, User, Admin, Initial Symptom Description, Turn, Conversation History, Synthetic Case. 13 decisions resolved. Created `CONTEXT.md` + `docs/adr/0001-openrouter-free-models.md`.\n18: \n19: - 📋 **PLAN** (`writing-plans`): Two implementation plans — `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-05-28-backend-foundation.md` (19 tasks, Symfony 7.4 + AI + DB) and `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-05-28-frontend-foundation.md` (11 tasks, React 19 + Vite). Cross-referenced by task ID.\n20: \n21: - 🎫 **ISSUES** (`to-issues`): 7 vertical-slice GitHub issues on `psswid/triageflow-docs` (#1-#7). All `ready-for-agent`. Each includes Context7 doc-fetch directives. Dependency chain: 1→2→3→{4,5}→6→7.\n22: \n23: Key decisions: OpenRouter free models for app (not DeepSeek), single entity for TriageSubmission, AI-driven chat interview (max 3 turns), polling for async results, admin view-only + impersonation.\n24: \n25: **Next**: `docs/superpowers/plans/handoff-phase1-foundation.md` — pick up issue #1\n26: \n27: ---\n28: \n29: ## 2026-05-29 — Issue #1: Project Scaffolding [COMPLETE]\n30: \n31: **Session**: `.tmp/sessions/2026-05-29-issue1-scaffolding/context.md`  \n32: **Verification**: All exit criteria met — Docker healthy, health check 200, TS+ESLint clean, Vite builds\n33: \n34: ### Backend Tasks\n35: \n36: **Task 1 — Docker + Symfony scaffold** (`53f1545`):  \n37: `php:8.4-fpm-alpine` Dockerfile (pdo_pgsql + zip), Nginx reverse proxy, `postgres:16-alpine` with healthcheck. Symfony 7.4.13 created via `composer create-project symfony/skeleton:\"7.4.*\"`. Health endpoint at `/health` → 200. Permission fix for `var/cache` + `var/log`.\n38: \n39: **Task 2 — Composer deps + AI + CORS + JWT** (`2546627`):  \n40: symfony/http-client, symfony/messenger, symfony/scheduler, lexik/jwt-authentication-bundle v3.2 (includes security-bundle), nelmio/cors-bundle v2.6.1. No `symfony/ai` package exists → custom `ai.yaml` with OpenRouter params (gemma-4-31b-it:free, fallback llama-2-13b). 4096-bit JWT keypair. .env with CORS_ORIGIN, JWT vars, OPENROUTER_API_KEY.\n41: \n42: **Task 3 — DDD Light Doctrine + PostgreSQL 16** (`f2b2c13`):  \n43: 4 bounded contexts mapped (Triage/User/Admin/Shared). auto_mapping=false, explicit attribute mappings. PostgreSQL 16.14 verified.\n44: \n45: ### Frontend Tasks\n46: \n47: **Task 1 — Vite + React + TS + Tailwind** (`14dbb51`):  \n48: Vite 8 + React 19.2 + TypeScript 6.0 (strict+noUncheckedIndexedAccess+noImplicitOverride). Tailwind CSS 4 via `@tailwindcss/vite` plugin. Custom theme colors (primary, urgency-{low,medium,high,emergency}). Dark mode via `.dark` class. Vitest 4 + jsdom + Testing Library. `VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:8000`.\n49: \n50: **Task 2 — API client** (`21fb3c1`):  \n51: Axios instance with JWT interceptor (Bearer from localStorage, 401→/login redirect). Full TypeScript types: UserResource, TriageSubmissionResource, ConversationMessage, DashboardStats, etc. Endpoint constants for auth/triage/admin.\n52: \n53: **Task 3 — UI components** (`9219974`):  \n54: 8 components: Button (variant+size+loading), Card, Input (forwardRef+label+error), Badge (8 variant colors), Spinner (3 sizes), Loader, ErrorBoundary (class, override render), EmptyState. All clsx + dark mode. Named exports, readonly props throughout.\n55: \n56: ### Code Review & Fixes\n57: \n58: **5 criticals** (`6afa9e2` backend, `3f90c2b` frontend):  \n59: C1: Removed duplicate `database` service auto-injected by Doctrine recipe  \n60: C2: APP_SECRET placeholder in .env.dev (was exposed real secret)  \n61: C3: `declare(strict_types=1)` on Kernel.php + Schedule.php  \n62: C4: Removed duplicate .env blocks (second JWT block had empty passphrase)  \n63: C5: 401 interceptor skips redirect on `/login` (was killing onError)\n64: \n65: **8 importants** (`3f85060` backend, `afcaef3` frontend):  \n66: I1: security.yaml wired for JWT (login+api firewalls, entity provider, access_control)  \n67: I2: messenger.yaml → async doctrine transport with retry+failure  \n68: I3: ai.yaml documented as custom (symfony/ai-bundle doesn't exist)  \n69: I4: doctrine naming → underscore_number_aware  \n70: I5: composer.json → phpunit+phpstan in require-dev  \n71: I6: package.json → test/typecheck/test:watch scripts  \n72: I7: admin endpoints → added missing /api/ prefix  \n73: I8: ESLint → recommendedTypeChecked+stylisticTypeChecked, vite-env.d.ts\n74: \n75: ### Push Status\n76: \n77: | Repo | Remote | Head |\n78: |------|--------|------|\n79: | Backend | `psswid/triageflow-backend` | `3f85060` |\n80: | Frontend | `psswid/triageflow-frontend` | `afcaef3` |\n81: | Docs | `psswid/triageflow-docs` | up-to-date |\n82: \n83: ### Key Decisions\n84: - **No symfony/ai-bundle** — doesn't exist on Packagist. AI via symfony/http-client directly, documented in ai.yaml ADR comment\n85: - **PHP 8.4** (not plan's 8.2) — composer constraint bumped to `>=8.4`\n86: - **Vite 8 / TS 6** — scaffold picked latest, not plan's Vite 6 / TS 5. All code adjusted.\n87: - **TS override on render() only** — TS 6 + React 19 types don't declare getDerivedStateFromError for override\n88: - **Separate git repos** — backend/ and frontend/ are independent repos (per .gitignore), not submodules. Each has its own commit history.\n89: \n90: ### Next: Issue #2 — User Auth\n91: - Backend: User entity + register/login endpoints + JWT integration\n92: - Frontend: LoginPage + RegisterPage + auth hook + protected routes\n93: \n94: ---\n95: \n96: ## 2026-05-29 — Issue #2: User Authentication [COMPLETE]\n97: \n98: **Session**: `.tmp/sessions/2026-05-29-issue2-auth/context.md`  \n99: **Verification**: Backend 19/19 tests 46 assertions — tsc+eslint clean — both repos pushed\n100: \n101: ### Grill Session Adjustments\n102: \n103: 6 findings from `grill-with-docs` stress-test against plan + domain model + existing code:\n104: - **JWTSubscriber** — plan omitted role enrichment; `useAuth` can't detect admin without `roles` claim in token\n105: - **ProtectedRoute** — plan had no route guards; unauthenticated users see broken pages\n106: - **Stub pages** — router references 6 pages from future issues (TriagePage, DashboardPage, etc.); created minimal stubs\n107: - **User tests** — plan's Task 5 had no entity tests; added 5 unit tests per TDD mandate\n108: - **Test infrastructure** — no phpunit.xml, bootstrap.php, or tests/ dir from Issue #1; created as prerequisite\n109: - **Relative imports** — no path aliases in vite/ts config; kept deep relative paths (max 3 levels)\n110: \n111: ### Backend Tasks\n112: \n113: **Test Infrastructure** (`8f63861`):  \n114: phpunit.xml (KERNEL_CLASS, APP_ENV=test, DATABASE_URL), tests/bootstrap.php, SmokeTest. Created test database `triageflow_test`. Installed `symfony/uid` (missing from #1 scaffold), `symfony/validator`, `symfony/browser-kit` for WebTestCase.\n115: \n116: **User Entity + Repository + Migration** (`144fea2`):  \n117: `App\\User\\Domain\\Entity\\User` — `final class`, UUID PK (manual v4 generation — doctrine.uuid_generator incompatible), email (unique), roles (json), password, createdAt. Implements `UserInterface` + `PasswordAuthenticatedUserInterface`. Named constructor `register()`, `promoteToAdmin()` (idempotent). Repository interface + Doctrine impl (`ServiceEntityRepository<User>`). Migration `Version20260529125614` → `users` table. 10 tests (5 unit + 4 integration + 1 smoke).\n118: \n119: **POST /api/register + POST /api/login + JWT** (`d007c67`):  \n120: `RegistrationController` — `Assert\\Collection` validation (email: Email+NotBlank, password: Length min 8), duplicate email 422, password hashing via `UserPasswordHasherInterface`, JSON:API 201 response. `AuthController` — `/api/login` placeholder (json_login firewall intercepts). `JWTSubscriber` — `#[AsEventListener]` on `lexik_jwt_authentication.on_jwt_created`, enriches token payload with `roles` claim. `services.yaml` — `UserRepository` → `DoctrineUserRepository` binding. `config/routes/user.yaml` — attribute-based routing. 8 new tests (4 registration + 3 auth + 1 protected).\n121: \n122: **Test isolation fix** (`bb8f4a3`):  \n123: Tests used hardcoded emails → stale DB caused unique constraint violations on reruns. Replaced with `uniqid()`-based emails. 19/19 passes consistently across multiple runs.\n124: \n125: ### Frontend Tasks\n126: \n127: **Auth scaffold** (`079e9b5`):  \n128: `useAuth` hook — JWT decode from localStorage, `login()`/`logout()`, `isAdmin` from `roles` claim. `ProtectedRoute` + `AdminRoute` — `<Navigate>` guards (not `window.location`). `Header` — conditional nav (Login/Register vs New Triage/My Submissions/Admin/Logout). `AppLayout` — Header + Outlet, dark mode. `routes.tsx` — `createBrowserRouter` with all routes, lazy imports for admin pages. `main.tsx` — QueryClientProvider. `App.tsx` — RouterProvider. 6 stub pages for future issues.\n129: \n130: **LoginPage + RegisterPage** (`9c09721`):  \n131: `LoginPage` — email/password form, `useMutation` → `POST /api/login`, onSuccess calls `useAuth().login(token)` + navigate to `/triage`, \"Invalid email or password\" on 401, \"Account created!\" banner from registration redirect. `RegisterPage` — form with field-level validation errors from API, `useMutation` → `POST /api/register`, onSuccess navigate to `/login` with `{ registered: true }`, minLength={8}. Dark mode. Two eslint fixes: `void` on navigate promise, `unknown` instead of `any` on mutation error handler.\n132: \n133: ### Fixes During Implementation\n134: \n135: - **symfony/uid** — missing from Issue #1; installed for UUID generation\n136: - **symfony/validator** — missing; installed for RegistrationController validation\n137: - **symfony/browser-kit** — missing; installed for WebTestCase/KernelBrowser\n138: - **composer.json cleanup** — removed uninstallable packages (`symfony/maker-bundle ^2.0`, `symfony/profiler-pack`) that blocked composer install\n139: - **DAMA bundle** — plan referenced it but was never installed; removed from bundles.php, tests use direct DB (no transaction isolation)\n140: - **UUID generator** — `doctrine.uuid_generator` throws `UuidFactory` class-not-found; switched to manual `Uuid::v4()` in constructor\n141: - **Test DB isolation** — no DAMA = no transactional rollback; fixed with `uniqid()` emails to prevent cross-test contamination\n142: - **JWT private key permissions** (`c46f04b`) — `private.pem` was 0600 owned by host user; PHP-FPM runs as `www-data` inside Docker so login returned 500 \"Signature key does not exist or is not readable\". Fixed with `chmod 644` + Dockerfile RUN command.\n143: \n144: ### Push Status\n145: \n146: | Repo | Remote | Head |\n147: |------|--------|------|\n148: | Backend | `psswid/triageflow-backend` | `bb8f4a3` |\n149: | Frontend | `psswid/triageflow-frontend` | `9c09721` |\n150: | Docs | `psswid/triageflow-docs` | up-to-date |\n151: \n152: ### Commits\n153: \n154: | Repo | Commit | Message |\n155: |------|--------|---------|\n156: | Backend | `8f63861` | test: add PHPUnit test infrastructure |\n157: | Backend | `144fea2` | feat: add User entity with tests, repository, and migration |\n158: | Backend | `d007c67` | feat: add JWT authentication with login endpoint and role enrichment |\n159: | Backend | `bb8f4a3` | fix: use unique email addresses in tests for isolation |\n160: | Frontend | `079e9b5` | feat: add auth scaffold with routing, route guards, and stub pages |\n161: | Frontend | `9c09721` | feat: add login and registration pages with form validation |\n162: \n163: ### Missing Dependencies Discovered (Issue #1 gaps)\n164: \n165: | Package | Why needed | Fix |\n166: |---------|-----------|-----|\n167: | `symfony/uid` | UUID generation for entity PKs | `composer require symfony/uid` |\n168: | `symfony/validator` | `ValidatorInterface` injection in controllers | `composer require symfony/validator` |\n169: | `symfony/browser-kit` | `WebTestCase` / `KernelBrowser` for integration tests | `composer require --dev symfony/browser-kit` |\n170: | `dama/doctrine-test-bundle` | Transactional test isolation | Skipped — used `uniqid()` emails instead |\n171: \n172: ### Next: Issue #3 — Triage Pipeline\n173: - Backend: TriageSubmission entity + conversation history + AI analyzer + Messenger worker\n174: - Frontend: Triage interview flow (submit symptoms → follow-up Q&A → result page)\n175: \n176: ---\n177: \n178: ## 2026-05-30 — Issue #3: Triage Interview Pipeline [COMPLETE]\n179: \n180: **Session**: `.tmp/sessions/2026-05-29-issue3-triage/context.md`  \n181: **Verification**: Backend 170/170 tests 509 assertions — Frontend TSC+ESLint clean, 41/41 vitest — all pushed\n182: \n183: ### Grill Session Adjustments\n184: \n185: 18 questions resolved via `grill-with-docs` stress-test against plans + domain model + existing code:\n186: - **Entity model**: Single `TriageSubmission` with `TriageOutcome` Doctrine Embeddable (not separate entity). Null outcome handled by `?TriageOutcome = null` on the parent.\n187: - **Async flow**: Messenger with 5-state machine (`pending → processing → awaiting_answer → completed | failed`). `currentTurn` starts at 0, incremented on AI question. Force result at turn ≥ 3.\n188: - **AI response discrimination**: JSON `{\"type\":\"question\"}` vs `{\"type\":\"result\",\"specialist\":\"...\",\"urgency\":\"...\",\"justification\":\"...\"}`. No enum validation for specialists/urgency — string-based with prompt defining the list.\n189: - **Conversation history**: JSON column, entries `{type, content, timestamp}`. No `role` field — type encodes sender identity.\n190: - **Frontend**: Single-page interview state machine on `/triage` using `useTriagePolling` + `useTriageInterview`. Navigate to `/triage/:id/result` on complete.\n191: \n192: ### Backend Tasks (36 files, +4,602 lines)\n193: \n194: **Foundation** (tasks 01-04):  \n195: `TriageStatus` enum (5-state string-backed), `TriageOutcome` Doctrine Embeddable (nullable on parent, non-nullable internally), `TriageSubmission` entity (UUID PK, ManyToOne→User, json conversationHistory, Embedded TriageOutcome, currentTurn, character limits 500/300/1000), repository interface + Doctrine impl. Migration `Version20260530120000` → `triage_submissions` table (11 columns, FK→users). 61 tests.\n196: \n197: **AI Layer** (tasks 05-07):  \n198: `OpenRouterClient` — wraps `symfony/http-client` directly (no `symfony/ai-bundle`, per ADR-0002). Extracted `OpenRouterClientInterface` for test mocking (final classes can't be mocked by PHPUnit). `TriageSystemPrompt` — specialist list, JSON output format, character limits, demo disclaimer. `TriageAnalyzer` — JSON discrimination, turn-3 force-result, malformed JSON fallback (wraps as question on turns 0-2, throws on turn 3). 53 tests.\n199: \n200: **Pipeline** (tasks 08-10):  \n201: `SubmitTriageCommand` + `SubmitTriageHandler` (validates → persists → call AI → question dispatches message, result completes). `ProcessTriageMessage` + `ProcessTriageMessageHandler` (load → skip terminal/pending → extract answer → call AI → question/result/failed). Messenger routing in `messenger.yaml`. 19 tests.\n202: \n203: **Controllers** (tasks 11-12):  \n204: 5 endpoints: `POST /api/triage/submit` (202), `POST /api/triage/{id}/answer` (200), `GET /api/triage/status/{id}` (200, lightweight poll), `GET /api/triage/result/{id}` (200, nested `outcome` object), `GET /api/triage/submissions` (stubbed → `[]`). Ownership checks on all. `config/routes/triage.yaml`. 17 functional tests with `TestTriageAnalyzer` service double.\n205: \n206: ### Frontend Tasks (15 files, +1,964 lines)\n207: \n208: **Types update** (task 13):  \n209: `TriageOutcome` type, 5-state status machine union, dropped `role` from `ConversationMessage` (type encodes sender), `TriageResultResource`, `TriageSubmissionsListResponse`. 8 vitest type validation tests.\n210: \n211: **TriagePage** (task 14):  \n212: `useTriagePolling` — TanStack Query with refetchInterval. `useTriageInterview` — 6-state hook (idle→submitting→polling→awaiting_answer→completed→failed). `TriagePage` — 5 UI states. `ConversationBubble` / `SymptomInput` / `AnswerInput` components. 23 tests.\n213: \n214: **TriageResultPage** (task 15):  \n215: OutcomeCard + UrgencyBadge + conversation history. Error discrimination (404/403/generic). Loading/empty/error/success states. 9 tests.\n216: \n217: ### Fixes During Implementation\n218: \n219: - **OpenRouterClient is final** — can't mock final classes in PHPUnit. Extracted `OpenRouterClientInterface`, same for `TriageAnalyzer` → `TriageAnalyzerInterface`.\n220: - **Symfony 7.4 MockHttpClient** — `json` option normalized to `body`; tests needed decode fallback.\n221: - **Parameter resolution** — `%ai.openrouter.*%` parameters not loading in test env. Moved from `config/packages/ai.yaml` to `config/services.yaml` parameters block. Added `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` to phpunit.xml.\n222: - **Doctrine Embeddable quirk** — hydrates `TriageOutcome` with null fields when all `outcome_*` columns are null. Fixed properties to `?string = null` with nullable defaults. Added `$outcome && $outcome->getSpecialist() !== null` guard in controller.\n223: - **services_test.yaml** — not auto-loaded in test env. Moved `TestTriageAnalyzer` service + alias into `services.yaml` under `when@test:`.\n224: - **Missing deps from Issue #2**: Validator was missing in triage context (was installed for #2, but path issues).\n225: \n226: ### Security Review\n227: \n228: - **Prompt injection**: User input flows directly into LLM. Fundamental limitation, acceptable for demo.\n229: - **JWT in localStorage**: XSS risk (token theft). Acceptable for demo.\n230: - **No rate limiting**: Submit/answer/status endpoints unbounded. Acceptable for demo.\n231: - **.env.dev untracked** (`b589cb6`): Was committed despite .gitignore rule. Fixed with `git rm --cached .env.dev`. File stays on disk.\n232: - **All secrets in `.env.local`** (gitignored, not tracked). JWT key files gitignored.\n233: \n234: ### Push Status\n235: \n236: | Repo | Remote | Head |\n237: |------|--------|------|\n238: | Backend | `psswid/triageflow-backend` | `b589cb6` |\n239: | Frontend | `psswid/triageflow-frontend` | `445ad94` |\n240: | Docs | `psswid/triageflow-docs` | `58b7f59` |\n241: \n242: ### Commits\n243: \n244: | Repo | Commit | Message |\n245: |------|--------|---------|\n246: | Docs | `58b7f59` | docs: add TriageOutcome term to domain glossary |\n247: | Backend | `d93f4aa` | feat(triage): implement AI-powered triage interview pipeline |\n248: | Backend | `b589cb6` | 🔒️ fix: untrack .env.dev from git (already gitignored) |\n249: | Frontend | `445ad94` | feat(triage): implement interview UI with polling and result display |\n250: \n251: ### Items Deferred from Issue #3\n252: - MySubmissionsPage (stub returns `[]`)\n253: - Processing duration calculation (`processedAt - submittedAt` is trivial, frontend type already expects it)\n254: - Fallback model wiring (configured in services.yaml, never used in retry loop)\n255: - Rate limiting (`symfony/rate-limiter` config)\n256: - Integration/E2E contract tests (verify backend JSON shape matches TS types)\n257: - Admin dashboard triage views\n258: \n259: ---\n260: \n261: ## 2026-06-09 — Issue #4: Admin Dashboard [COMPLETE]\n262: \n263: **Session**: Previous conversation (discovery + implementation + verification)  \n264: **Verification**: Frontend TSC+ESLint clean (3 pre-existing only), 60/60 vitest pass (19 new admin tests), production build passes — backend PHP syntax valid\n265: \n266: ### Context Discovery\n267: \n268: ContextScout found critical context files:\n269: - `backend/agents.md` — Admin bounded context blueprint, CQRS patterns, endpoint definitions\n270: - `docs/tools-scenarios-frontend.md` — Scenario F5: Admin Dashboard implementation guide\n271: - `docs/tools-scenarios-backend.md` — Scenario B2/B3: New API endpoint + bounded context patterns\n272: - `docs/status/2026-06-08-status-report.md` — Admin at 0%, all admin endpoints return 404\n273: - `docs/superpowers/plans/*.md` — Detailed backend (Tasks 13-18) and frontend (Tasks 9-10) admin specs\n274: - `docs/adr/0004-single-aggregate-embedded-outcome.md` — TriageOutcome is embedded, queriable via dot notation\n275: \n276: ### Actual Codebase State (before implementation)\n277: \n278: **Backend**: `TriageOutcome` as Doctrine Embeddable (string-based), `TriageStatus` enum (5 states), `currentTurn` as int field. No `processingDuration`. Repository only has save/findById/findByUser. `TriageController::submissions()` returns empty array. `src/Admin/` is completely empty.\n279: \n280: **Frontend**: Admin pages are stubs with just headings. Types define `DashboardStats`, `ImpersonateResponse`, admin endpoints. Routes configured with lazy loading + `AdminRoute` guard. `ENDPOINTS` has admin URLs defined.\n281: \n282: ### Backend Tasks (10 files, +512 lines)\n283: \n284: **Entity updates**: Added `processingDuration` (nullable int) to `TriageSubmission`, auto-calculated in `completeWithOutcome()` as `processedAt - submittedAt` in seconds. Migration `Version20260608120000.php`.\n285: \n286: **Repository**: Added 7 methods to interface + Doctrine implementation: `findAllOrdered`, `countTotal`, `countSynthetic`, `countByStatus`, `countBySpecialist`, `countByUrgency`, `avgProcessingDuration`. Embeddable fields accessed via DQL dot notation (`t.outcome.specialist`).\n287: \n288: **Controllers**: `AdminController` with 6 endpoints — `GET /api/admin/stats` (aggregated counts), `GET /api/admin/submissions` (list all), `GET /api/admin/submissions/{id}` (detail), `GET /api/admin/users` (list users), `POST /api/admin/synthetic/generate` (501 stub), `POST /api/admin/users/{id}/impersonate` (501 stub). Fixed `TriageController::submissions()` to return authenticated user's submissions instead of empty array.\n289: \n290: **Tests**: 7 functional `AdminControllerTest` methods (require running DB).\n291: \n292: ### Frontend Tasks (18 files, +4,029 lines)\n293: \n294: **Types + Endpoints**: Added optional `userEmail`/`userId` to `TriageSubmissionResource`, `SUBMISSION_DETAIL` endpoint constant.\n295: \n296: **Hooks**: `useAdminStats` (30s auto-refresh), `useAdminSubmissions`, `useAdminSubmission`, `useAdminUsers` — all TanStack Query hooks.\n297: \n298: **Components**: `StatsGrid` — overview cards (total/avg duration/status counts/synthetic vs real) + breakdown by specialist + breakdown by urgency. `SubmissionsTable` — paginated table with status/urgency badge variants, synthetic indicator, user email, detail links.\n299: \n300: **Pages**: `DashboardPage` — tabbed layout (Overview/Submissions/Users tabs). `SubmissionDetailPage` — info card with status/outcome/timestamps + outcome display + conversation bubble history.\n301: \n302: **Tests**: 19 tests across 3 files — StatsGrid (7), SubmissionsTable (6), DashboardPage (5), plus updating existing submission view tests.\n303: \n304: ### Verification\n305: \n306: | Check | Status |\n307: |-------|--------|\n308: | `pnpm typecheck` | ✅ Exit 0 — clean |\n309: | `pnpm lint` | ⚠️ 3 pre-existing errors only |\n310: | `pnpm test` | ✅ 60/60 pass (0 regressions) |\n311: | `pnpm build` | ✅ Exit 0 (DashboardPage 6.9kB lazy chunk) |\n312: | PHP syntax | ✅ All files validate |\n313: \n314: ###