(resolved all 5)\n625: \n626: ### Fix 3 — PHPStan level 5\n627: - Installed `phpstan/phpstan`, `phpstan/phpstan-symfony`, `phpstan/phpstan-doctrine`, `phpstan/phpstan-phpunit`\n628: - Created `phpstan.neon.dist` with `treatPhpDocTypesAsCertain: false`\n629: - Fixed 40 errors (3 redundant null checks in `TriageAnalyzer.php`, 37 in tests)\n630: - Result: **0 errors at level 5**\n631: \n632: ### Fix 4 — ConversationBubble component test\n633: - 6 tests: user alignment (right), assistant alignment (left), result badge, content rendering, timestamp presence, initial_description alignment\n634: - Result: **87 frontend tests pass (12 files)**\n635: \n636: ### Pushed\n637: | Repo | Head | Message |\n638: |------|------|---------|\n639: | Backend | `4166fe2` | fix(testing): install symfony/mailer, add PHPStan level 5, fix test quality issues |\n640: | Frontend | `25cbdb9` | test(triage): add ConversationBubble component tests — and `affdcaf` for DashboardPage wrapper |\n641: \n642: ### Issue #7 Closed\n643: All 10 acceptance criteria met, issue closed via `gh issue close 7`.\n644: \n645: ---\n646: \n647: ## 2026-06-13 — Issue #10: Structured Logging + Observability [COMPLETE]\n648: \n649: **Session**: OpenAgent — grill → implement → code review → fix → push  \n650: **Verification**: Frontend 95/95 tests, TSC+ESLint clean. Backend 180/180 unit tests, PHPStan level 5 clean. Infrastructure-dependent 45 tests skipped (no PostgreSQL).\n651: \n652: ### Grill Session (`grill-with-docs`, compressed)\n653: \n654: Resolved all design decisions for structured logging:\n655: - **Correlation IDs**: UUID v4 via `Uuid::v4()->toRfc4122()`, static processor (not request-scoped)\n656: - **Subscriber**: HTTP `kernel.request`/`kernel.response` — handlers set own UUID in worker context\n657: - **OpenRouterClient**: `?LoggerInterface $logger = null` (optional, NullLogger in tests)\n658: - **Log field naming**: snake_case for JSON output\n659: - **Monolog processor**: default (all handlers/channels, no restriction)\n660: - **Handler status**: named string per return path (`noop_*`, `analysis_failed`, `success`, `error`)\n661: \n662: ### Backend Implementation\n663: \n664: **New files** (3):\n665: - `src/Shared/Infrastructure/Logging/CorrelationIdProcessor.php` — Monolog processor, `__invoke(LogRecord): LogRecord`, sets `$record->extra['correlation_id']`\n666: - `src/Shared/Infrastructure/Logging/CorrelationIdSubscriber.php` — `#[AsEventListener]` for kernel.request (priority 100, UUID gen) + kernel.response (X-Correlation-Id header)\n667: - `tests/Shared/Infrastructure/Logging/CorrelationIdSubscriberTest.php` — 6 tests (UUID format, sub-request skip, header presence/absence/skip)\n668: \n669: **Modified files** (8):\n670: - `config/services.yaml` — `monolog.processor` tag registration\n671: - `OpenRouterClient.php` — Optional logger with timing, primary-429 warning, retry-notice, rate-limit-all error, token_usage extraction\n672: - `ProcessTriageMessageHandler.php` — LoggerInterface + timing + status tracking\n673: - `ProcessSyntheticCaseMessageHandler.php` — Same, plus terminal state guard\n674: - `ProcessSyntheticTurnMessageHandler.php` — Same, with `failed_empty_answer` naming\n675: - `OpenRouterClientTest.php` — Added `logger: null` to named constructor args\n676: - 2 handler tests — LoggerInterface mock injection\n677: \n678: **Bug found & fixed**: `CorrelationIdProcessor` typed `array $record` but Monolog 3 passes `LogRecord` objects. Changed to `LogRecord` with `$record->extra['correlation_id']` mutation.\n679: \n680: **PHP 8.5 quirk**: Named arguments can't skip optional params before required ones. Moved `$logger` after all required params in `OpenRouterClient` constructor. Also fixed PHPStan `parameter.requiredAfterOptional`.\n681: \n682: ### Frontend Lint Fixes (same session)\n683: \n684: Cleaned 12 ESLint errors across 7 files:\n685: - `AuthProvider.tsx` — Removed redundant JWT expiry checks from `useEffect` (already in `useState` initializer)\n686: - `VerifyEmailPage.tsx` — Moved `!token` early return to `useState` initializer\n687: - `useAdminFailedMessages.ts` / `useGenerateSyntheticCase.ts` — Added `void` to floating `invalidateQueries` promises + typed API response\n688: - `FailedMessagesTable.tsx` — Removed unused import\n689: - `ImpersonateButton.test.tsx` — `eslint-disable` for intentional empty executor\n690: - `eslint.config.js` — Ignored playwright config + e2e specs\n691: \n692: ### Code Review Outcomes\n693: \n694: 5 Important + 1 Minor fixed:\n695: | # | Issue | Fix |\n696: |---|-------|-----|\n697: | 1 | Missing terminal guard in ProcessSyntheticCaseMessageHandler | Added `noop_already_terminal` guard |\n698: | 2 | Missing warning on primary model 429 | Added `$this->logger?->warning(...)` |\n699: | 3 | Missing notice on transport retry success | Conditional notice vs info based on `$attempts > 0` |\n700: | 4 | `empty_answer` naming inconsistent | Renamed → `failed_empty_answer` |\n701: | 5 | `rate_limited_all_models` used warning (spec said error) | Changed to `error` |\n702: | 6 | `$status = 'noop'` unreachable | Changed to defensive `'noop_already_terminal'` |\n703: \n704: ### Commits\n705: \n706: | Repo | Commit | Message |\n707: |------|--------|---------|\n708: | Backend | `fea218d` | feat: add structured logging with correlation IDs |\n709: | Frontend | `3b0a0aa` | fix: resolve ESLint errors across auth, admin hooks, and tests |\n710: \n711: ### Push Status\n712: \n713: | Repo | Remote | Head |\n714: |------|--------|------|\n715: | Backend | `psswid/triageflow-backend` | `fea218d` |\n716: | Frontend | `psswid/triageflow-frontend` | `3b0a0aa` |\n717: | Docs | `psswid/triageflow-docs` | up-to-date |\n718: \n719: ---\n720: \n721: ## 2026-06-12 — CI Pipeline: Backend CI Fixed (5 iterations) [COMPLETE]\n722: \n723: **Two workflow files created** — `backend/.github/workflows/ci.yml` (3 jobs) + `frontend/.github/workflows/ci.yml` (2 jobs).\n724: \n725: **Frontend CI passed immediately** ✅ — Vitest 87 tests + TypeScript typecheck.\n726: \n727: **Backend CI required 5 fixes across 4 commits:**\n728: \n729: | # | Fix | Issue |\n730: |---|-----|-------|\n731: | 1 | `cp .env.test .env` before `composer install` | `.env` missing in CI checkout (gitignored) |\n732: | 2 | `--no-scripts` flag + `.env` creation after install | `cache:clear` auto-script fails without `.env` |\n733: | 3 | `DEFAULT_URI` env var added | Needed by `routing.yaml` + `services.yaml` at boot |\n734: | 4 | `CORS_ALLOW_ORIGIN`, `MESSENGER_TRANSPORT_DSN`, `MAILER_DSN`, `JWT_*` | All needed at runtime, not in `.env.test` |\n735: | 5 | `JWT_PASSPHRASE=` (empty) | OpenSSL 3.x on ubuntu-latest rejects non-empty passphrase on unencrypted PKCS#8 key (`DECODER routines::unsupported`) |\n736: | 6 | `openssl genpkey` in CI | JWT keys not tracked in git — don't exist in checkout |\n737: | 7 | `Length(min: 8)` named args | Symfony 7.3 deprecation triggers `failOnDeprecation=\"true\"` |\n738: | 8 | `coverage: pcov` (was `none`) | \"No coverage driver\" warning triggers `failOnWarning=\"true\"` |\n739: \n740: **Final state**: ✅ All 3 jobs green — 228 tests / 771 assertions in 62s, PHPStan level 5 clean in 16s, Docker build in 42s.\n741: \n742: **ADR-0007 created** — documents the decision to generate JWT keys at runtime in CI rather than committing them.\n743: \n744: ---\n745: \n746: ## 2026-06-12 — Issue #9: Worker Monitoring + Failed Messages [COMPLETE]\n747: \n748: **Plan**: `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-12-failed-messages.md`  \n749: **Verification**: Backend 236/236 tests (797 assertions), Frontend 95/95 tests (13 files), TypeScript zero errors — all merged to `master`\n750: \n751: ### Design Decisions (via `grill-with-docs`)\n752: \n753: | # | Question | Decision |\n754: |---|----------|----------|\n755: | Q1 | Failed Messages vs Dead Letter Queue | **Failed Messages** (aligns with Symfony's `failed` transport) |\n756: | Q2 | HealthController location | Standalone at `App\\Controller` (cross-cutting) |\n757: | Q3 | Retry/Delete approach vs service layer | **Raw SQL** via DBAL\\Connection (matches GET approach) |\n758: | Q4 | FailedMessagesTable pattern | **Self-fetching** (like UsersTable) |\n759: | Q5 | Endpoint location | `AdminController` (not separate controller) |\n760: | Q6 | Tab placement | New \"Failed Messages\" tab (not panel within Overview) |\n761: | Q7a | Data model | `FailedMessageResource` with `preview` (extracted from body) |\n762: | Q7b | Retry/Delete UX | **Inline buttons** (blue Retry + red Delete, confirm dialog) |\n763: | Q7c | Polling interval | **15s** |\n764: \n765: ### Backend Changes\n766: \n767: **AdminController.php** (+100 lines, 3 endpoints):\n768: - `GET /api/admin/failed-messages` — queries `messenger_messages WHERE queue_name = 'failed'`, returns JSON:API-style with type/error/preview/timestamp\n769: - `POST /api/admin/failed-messages/{id}/retry` — **atomic UPDATE** `SET queue_name = 'default', delivered_at = NULL WHERE id = :id AND queue_name = 'failed'`, checks affected row count for 404\n770: - `DELETE /api/admin/failed-messages/{id}` — **atomic DELETE** `WHERE id = :id AND queue_name = 'failed'`, checks affected row count for 404\n771: \n772: Key fixes from code review:\n\n(Output capped at 50 KB. Showing lines 1-772. Use offset=773 to continue.)\n</content>",
