          "type": "text",
          "text": "Here's your accessibility audit guide. This is a **HITL (human-in-the-loop) process** — you drive, I support by finding code and suggesting fixes. I won't implement anything without your explicit sign-off.\n\n---\n\n## Step 1: Set up the audit environment\n\n```bash\n# Terminal 1: backend\ncd backend && symfony serve -d\n\n# Terminal 2: frontend  \ncd frontend && npm run dev\n```\n\n---\n\n## Step 2: Choose your audit tool\n\nYou have 3 options, pick one:\n\n| Tool | Effort | What it gives you |\n|------|--------|-------------------|\n| **A) axe DevTools browser extension** | 1 min setup | One-click automated WCAG violations per page |\n| **B) Lighthouse in Chrome DevTools** | 0 setup (built-in) | Accessibility score + violations list |\n| **C) Manual keyboard/screen reader** | 15-30 min | Real user experience beyond what automation catches |\n\n**Recommendation**: Use **A) axe DevTools** for the fast sweep, then spot-check key user flows with **C) manual testing**.\n\n---\n\n## Step 3: The audit checklist (10 points per page)\n\nBased on your existing handoff at `docs/handoffs/handoff-2026-06-13-ux-polish-phase1.md`. Go through each of these **9 pages**:\n\n| # | Page | Route |\n|---|------|-------|\n| 1 | Login | `/login` |\n| 2 | Register | `/register` |\n| 3 | Verify Email | `/verify-email` |\n| 4 | Triage | `/app/triage` |\n| 5 | Triage Result | `/app/submissions/:id` |\n| 6 | My Submissions | `/app/submissions` |\n| 7 | Submission Detail | `/app/submissions/:id` (authenticated view) |\n| 8 | Admin Dashboard | `/admin/dashboard` |\n| 9 | Admin Submission Detail | `/admin/submissions/:id` |\n\nFor each page, check:\n\n- [ ] **Keyboard**: Can Tab through every interactive element? Is the order logical?\n- [ ] **Focus visible**: Do you see a focus ring on every element you Tab to?\n- [ ] **Semantic HTML**: Headings go h1 → h2 → h3 (no skips)? Landmarks used?\n- [ ] **ARIA labels**: Icon-only buttons have `aria-label`? Dynamic regions have live announcements?\n- [ ] **Color contrast**: 4.5:1 for body text, 3:1 for large text (use axe DevTools for this)\n- [ ] **Screen reader**: Does dynamic content get announced? (polling updates, errors, toasts)\n- [ ] **Touch targets**: Interactive elements at least 44×44px?\n- [ ] **Motion**: Does `prefers-reduced-motion` suppress animations? (currently **not implemented**)\n- [ ] **Design consistency**: Spacing, typography, colors aligned with design tokens?\n- [ ] **Loading states**: Skeleton variants match the actual content layout?\n\n---\n\n## Step 4: Your role vs my role\n\n**You (human reviewer):**\n- Navigate through the app with keyboard only (no mouse)\n- Run axe DevTools or Lighthouse on each page\n- Use VoiceOver or NVDA for screen reader test on 2-3 key flows\n- Decide what's worth fixing vs deferring\n\n**Me (agent supporter):**\n- When you find something: tell me the page + issue, I'll find the exact file/line\n- I'll propose fixes → you approve → I implement\n- I won't touch anything without your sign-off\n\n---\n\n## Step 5: How to start\n\nQuickest path:\n\n1. Install [axe DevTools](https://www.deque.com/axe/devtools/) (free browser extension)\n2. Open the first page at `localhost:5173/login`\n3. Click the axe tab → \"Scan all of my page\"\n4. Screenshot or note the violations\n5. Tell me: \"Page X has Y violations\" and I'll find the code\n\nWant to start now, or prefer a different approach?",
