        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Good news: **`@axe-core/cli`** (the free open-source version) runs fine via `npx`. But for a React SPA it only captures the initial HTML — not the real rendered DOM. So here's the free-tool plan:\n\n---\n\n## Free open-source accessibility audit toolkit\n\n### 1. Lighthouse — built into Chrome (zero install)\n\nOpen your app at `localhost:5173/login`, hit **F12 → Lighthouse tab**, uncheck everything except **Accessibility**, run. Gives you a score (0-100) + a flat list of violations per page. Completely free, no trial, no account.\n\n### 2. Add `eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y` — catches issues at code level\n\nThis catches missing `alt`, unlabeled buttons, bad heading hierarchy, missing `aria-*` — right in your editor. I can add this to your ESLint config in ~2 minutes. It's the industry standard free static analysis for React a11y.\n\n### 3. Manual keyboard testing — the part automation misses\n\nNo tool substitute. Tab through each page, check focus visibility, check logical tab order.\n\n---\n\n| Tool | Cost | Catches |\n|------|------|---------|\n| Lighthouse | Free, built-in | Color contrast, ARIA, landmark structure, heading order, link names |\n| `eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y` | Free, npm | Missing labels, `alt` text, role issues, anchor/href misuse |\n| Manual keyboard | Free, your hands | Focus order, focus visibility, dynamic content announcements |\n\n---\n\n**Recommended plan:**\n\n1. I add `eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y` to your ESLint config right now (~2 min)\n2. You open each of the 9 pages in Chrome, run Lighthouse Accessibility audit\n3. You Tab through 2-3 key user flows (login → triage → result)\n4. Report findings to me → I propose fixes → you approve → I implement\n\nWant me to start with step 1 — adding the ESLint plugin?",
