              "prompt": "Fix 6 accessibility issues found by Lighthouse audit across 15 pages of the TriageFlow frontend. Each issue has been traced to specific files and lines.\n\n## Context\n- React 19 + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS 4 project at /home/stefan/dev/projects/triageflow/frontend\n- Dark mode is system-pref + localStorage toggle (dark class on `<html>`)\n- Design tokens: primary (blue), accent (teal), surface colors\n- 146 tests must keep passing, ESLint must stay clean for jsx-a11y\n\n---\n\n## Issue 1: \"Elements use prohibited ARIA attributes\" — 15/15 pages\n**File**: `src/components/ui/ToastProvider.tsx` lines 43-47\n**Problem**: `<div>` has `aria-label=\"Notifications\"` and `aria-live=\"polite\"` but no `role` attribute. `aria-label` is prohibited on a plain `<div>` per ARIA spec.\n**Fix**: Add `role=\"status\"` to the div. This is a live region for toast notifications — `role=\"status\"` is semantically correct for `aria-live=\"polite\"` containers.\n\n---\n\n## Issue 2: \"Insufficient color contrast\" — 14/15 pages\n\n### 2a. Register CTA button (all marketing pages)\n**Selectors**: `div.mx-auto > div.flex > div.hidden > a.rounded-lg`\n**File**: `src/components/layout/MarketingHeader.tsx` lines 55-60\n**Problem**: White text (#ffffff) on accent-500 (#14b8a6 = teal-500), contrast ratio 2.48 (need 4.5:1)\n**Fix**: Change `bg-accent-500` to `bg-accent-600` (teal-600 = #0d9488 — contrast 4.61:1). Also check `focus-visible:outline-accent-500` on same element, change to `focus-visible:outline-accent-600`.\n\n### 2b. Secondary text in dark mode cards (multiple pages)\n**Selectors**: `p.text-sm` (StatsGrid cards, marketing card descriptions)\n**Problem**: gray-500 (#6a7282) on near-black backgrounds (#101828, #030712), contrast 3.66-4.16 (need 4.5:1)\n**Investigate**: Search for all `text-gray-500` and `dark:text-gray-400` combinations used on dark backgrounds (`dark:bg-gray-900`, `dark:bg-gray-950`). The issue is body text colors. \n**Fix**: Where body text (14px normal weight) appears on dark card backgrounds, ensure contrast ≥ 4.5:1. Options:\n- Change `dark:text-gray-400` to `dark:text-gray-300` (lighter text → higher contrast)\n- Change `dark:text-gray-500` to `dark:text-gray-400`\n- This applies to card descriptions, stat labels, and similar secondary text on dark surfaces.\n**Files to check**: StatsGrid, FeatureCard, TechDecisionsGrid, StepCard, any component with card descriptions on dark backgrounds.\n\n### 2c. Login form submit button\n**Selector**: `button.inline-flex` (Login page submit button)\n**Problem**: White text on blue (#2b7fff), contrast 3.76\n**Fix**: Find the submit button on LoginPage — likely `bg-blue-600` or similar. Ensure it uses a shade dark enough for 4.5:1 with white text.\n\n### 2d. How It Works CTA button\n**Selector**: `main.flex-1 > div.max-w-4xl > div.mt-16 > a.inline-flex`\n**Problem**: White on teal (#14b8a6), contrast 2.48\n**Fix**: Same as 2a — change accent CTA buttons to accent-600.\n\n---\n\n## Issue 3: \"Document doesn't have `<title>`\" — 7 marketing pages\n**Pages**: about, contact, cookies, how-it-works, landing-page, privacy, terms\n**Files**: All 7 pages in `src/features/marketing/pages/*.tsx` use `<Helmet>` with `<title>`.\n**Problem**: `react-helmet-async` sets `<title>` via JS after hydration. Lighthouse checks before/at initial render when the `<title>` might not be set yet.\n**Fix**: In `index.html`, change `<title>Vite + React + TS</title>` to `<title>TriageFlow</title>` so there's always a fallback `<title>` before Helmet injects the page-specific one.\n\n---\n\n## Issue 4: \"Document does not have a main landmark\" — login, register, verify-email\n**Files**: \n- `src/features/auth/pages/LoginPage.tsx`\n- `src/features/auth/pages/RegisterPage.tsx`\n- `src/features/auth/pages/VerifyEmailPage.tsx`\n**Problem**: These pages render standalone (no MarketingLayout or AppLayout wrapper) and don't use a `<main>` element.\n**Fix**: Wrap the page content in a `<main>` tag (or add `role=\"main\"` to the outermost content wrapper div). Use `<main className=\"...\">` instead of `<div className=\"...\">` for the primary content container.\n\n---\n\n## Issue 5: \"Links rely on color to be distinguishable\" — login, register\n**Files**: \n- `src/features/auth/pages/LoginPage.tsx` line 70\n- `src/features/auth/pages/RegisterPage.tsx` line 68\n**Problem**: `<Link>` elements have `className=\"text-blue-600 hover:underline dark:text-blue-400\"` — underline only on hover. Lighthouse requires a non-color differentiator always visible.\n**Fix**: Add `underline` to the base class: `className=\"text-blue-600 underline hover:no-underline dark:text-blue-400\"` (underline by default, remove on hover for subtle polish — or just `underline` always).\n\n---\n\n## Issue 6: \"Heading elements not sequentially descending\" — admin, how-it-works\n### 6a. Admin Dashboard\n**File**: `src/features/admin/pages/DashboardPage.tsx` (or component)\n**Selector**: `div.space-y-6 > div.space-y-6 > div > h3.mb-2`\n**Problem**: Some section uses `<h3>` when the heading hierarchy jumped from `<h1>` to `<h3>` (missing `<h2>`).\n**Fix**: Check the heading structure — ensure headings go h1 → h2 → h3 with no skips. If the page doesn't have an h2, either add one or change the h3 to h2. If it's a card title within a section, ensure the section has a proper h2 first.\n\n### 6b. How It Works Page\n**File**: `src/features/marketing/pages/HowItWorksPage.tsx`\n**Selector**: `div.relative > div.flex > div.relative > h3.text-xl`\n**Problem**: h3 used where h2 should be (or heading order skipped).\n**Fix**: Audit the heading structure on this page. The StepCard component likely uses h3 for step titles. Ensure the parent page provides h2 headings before h3s.\n\n---\n\n## Verification\nAfter each fix:\n1. `npm run lint` — zero jsx-a11y violations\n2. `npm run test` — 146/146 tests pass\n3. `npm run build` — clean build\n\n## Important\n- Do NOT modify test files unless a component change requires it\n- Keep all existing functionality — these are markup/contrast fixes only\n- Do NOT create new files unless absolutely necessary\n- Report back: what you changed, which files, what the final lint + test results are",
