n  \n  \n\n\n\n\n    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n      \n    \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n  \n  \n  11. UX Polish: Loading states, error recovery, accessibility + design refresh #11New issueCopy linkNew issueCopy linkOpenOpen11. UX Polish: Loading states, error recovery, accessibility + design refresh#11Copy linkLabelsenhancementNew feature or requestNew feature or requestready-for-humanDescriptionpsswidopened on Jun 12, 2026Issue body actionsWhat to build\nElevate the frontend from \"functional demo\" to \"polished application\". Three layers: (1) loading states that feel responsive, (2) error boundaries that help users recover instead of hitting dead ends, (3) accessibility audit and fixes so the app is usable by keyboard-only and screen-reader users. Additionally, a full design refresh using the UI/UX design skill for a more \"real app\" feel across all views.\nThis is a HITL issue — the accessibility audit and design refresh produce decisions that need human review before implementation.\nScope\nLoading states (AFK-able):\n\nSkeleton loaders for TriagePage (while waiting for AI response / polling)\nSkeleton loaders for MySubmissionsPage (while fetching submission list)\nSkeleton loaders for DashboardPage stats grid (while loading stats)\nExisting Spinner component used appropriately for smaller loads\nNo layout shift when content loads (reserve space)\n\nError recovery (AFK-able):\n\nEnhanced ErrorBoundary with: retry button, \"go home\" fallback, error details toggle\nAPI error handling: toast/notification for transient errors, inline error for form submissions\nGraceful degradation: if stats fail to load, show \"unavailable\" card instead of blank\n\nAccessibility (requires audit → decisions):\n\nKeyboard navigation audit and fixes (all interactive elements reachable via Tab)\nFocus management for dynamic content (after form submit, after modal open, after route change)\nARIA labels: form inputs, buttons without visible text, live regions for status updates\nScreen reader: announcements for polling updates, status changes\n\nDesign refresh (requires human review):\n\nui-ux-pro-max skill review of all views (TriagePage, TriageResultPage, DashboardPage, MySubmissionsPage, LoginPage, RegisterPage, UsersPage, SubmissionDetailPage)\nConsistent spacing, typography, color usage across all views\n\"Real app\" feel: polish cards, tables, badges to look production-grade\n\nNot in scope\n\nResponsive mobile design (desktop-first is fine for this demo)\nAnimation library or complex transitions\nDark mode\n\nAcceptance criteria\n\n Skeleton loaders replace blank loading states on TriagePage, MySubmissionsPage, and DashboardPage\n ErrorBoundary offers retry and \"go home\" actions\n API errors surface as user-visible notifications (not silent failures)\n Keyboard Tab order is logical and all interactive elements are reachable\n Focus is managed after dynamic content changes (form submit, route change)\n ARIA labels exist on form inputs and icon-only buttons\n Live regions announce polling updates and status changes\n ui-ux-pro-max design review completed and approved by human\n All 87 frontend tests still pass\n\nBlocked by\nNone — can start immediately (but needs human sign-off at design review stage)Reactions are currently unavailableMetadataMetadataAssigneesNo one assignedLabelsenhancementNew feature or requestNew feature or requestready-for-humanProjectsNo projectsMilestoneNo milestoneRelationshipsNone yetDevelopmentNo branches or pull requestsIssue actions\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n    \n  \n\n  \n\n          \n  Footer\n\n  \n\n\n  \n    \n      \n        \n    \n\n\n      \n        © 2026 GitHub, Inc.\n      \n    \n\n    \n      Footer navigation\n\n      \n\n\n          \n            Terms\n          \n\n          \n            Privacy\n          \n\n          \n            Security\n          \n\n          \n            Status\n          \n\n          \n            Community\n          \n\n          \n            Docs\n          \n\n 