\n426: ### Key Components\n427: \n428: - **SyntheticSystemPrompt** — 7-domain symptom generator with \"DEMONSTRATION system\" disclaimer, 500-char limit\n429: - **ProcessSyntheticTurnMessageHandler** — `#[AsMessageHandler]`, idempotency guards for terminal states, calls OpenRouter for patient voice, extracts AI question from history\n430: - **GenerateSyntheticCaseHandler** — resolves system user from DB, retries symptom generation once on empty response, catches `TriageAnalysisFailedException` → marks submission `Failed`\n431: - **GenerateSyntheticCaseTask** — `#[AsCronTask('0 * * * *')]` via symfony/scheduler, delegates to handler\n432: - **ImpersonationController** — injects `JWTTokenManagerInterface::create()`, returns JWT for any user UUID\n433: \n434: ### Pre-existing Issues Fixed\n435: \n436: - **Admin tests returning 403**: `createAdminClient()` in `AdminControllerTest` created users without calling `promoteToAdmin()` — the test user never had `ROLE_ADMIN`. Fixed by adding explicit promotion.\n437: - **Test DB missing `processing_duration` column**: Schema was stale from Issue #4 migration. Fixed with `doctrine:schema:update --force --env=test`.\n438: - **Impersonation test double-booting kernel**: `testImpersonateReturns200()` was calling `$this->createClient()` twice. Fixed to single client creation.\n439: \n440: ### Code Review Outcomes\n441: \n442: | Issue | Finding | Fix |\n443: |-------|---------|-----|\n444: | I1 🟠 | Handler named `ProcessSyntheticTurnHandler` (codebase convention: `ProcessTriageMessageHandler`) | Renamed to `ProcessSyntheticTurnMessageHandler` |\n445: | I2 🟠 | `?MessageBusInterface $messageBus = null` silently skipped dispatch on misconfiguration | Made hard dependency (non-nullable) |\n446: | I3 🟠 | No unit tests for handler logic (endpoint-only coverage) | Deferred — endpoint tests cover primary flow |\n447: | I4 🟠 | `*/60 * * * *` non-standard cron syntax | Changed to `0 * * * *` |\n448: | I5 🟠 | No 403 test for non-admin on admin endpoints | Deferred — firewall covers globally |\n449: \n450: ### Verification\n451: \n452: | Check | Status |\n453: |-------|--------|\n454: | `php bin/phpunit` | ✅ 182/182 pass (552 assertions) |\n455: | `debug:router` | ✅ `api_admin_synthetic_generate` + `api_admin_impersonate` registered |\n456: | `debug:scheduler` | ✅ `0 * * * *` — next run at 13:00 |\n457: | System user in DB | ✅ `00000000-...` / `system@triageflow.local` / `ROLE_SYSTEM` |\n458: | Old 501 stubs removed | ✅ `AdminController` no longer has `generateSynthetic()` or `impersonate()` |\n459: \n460: ### Merge Status\n461: \n462: | Repo | Branch | Head |\n463: |------|--------|------|\n464: | Backend | `master` | `af653b8` (fast-forward merged, branch deleted) |\n465: | Docs | `master` | `03255c7` (no code changes needed) |\n466: \n467: ### ADRs Created\n468: \n469: - **ADR-0006** (`docs/adr/0006-system-user-sentinel-uuid.md`) — Documents the system user design: fixed UUID `00000000-...`, `ROLE_SYSTEM`, empty password, migration-based seed vs `findOrCreate` at runtime. Meets all three ADR criteria (hard to reverse, surprising without context, real trade-off).\n470: \n471: ### Post-Merge Live E2E Test\n472: \n473: Manually triggered `POST /api/admin/synthetic/generate` via curl against running Docker stack. Full pipeline verified end-to-end:\n474: \n475: 1. **Symptom generation** (OpenRouter via `SyntheticSystemPrompt`): *\"Sharp, stabbing pain in lower back radiating to left calf, 7/10 severity\"*\n476: 2. **Initial AI analysis** (`TriageAnalyzer::analyzeInitial`): Asked follow-up question — *\"Numbness/tingling/weakness or bowel/bladder changes?\"*\n477: 3. **Patient answer** (10s delayed via `ProcessSyntheticTurnMessageHandler` + `DelayStamp(10000)`): *\"Tingling in left calf, no bowel/bladder issues\"*\n478: 4. **Final outcome** (`TriageAnalyzer::analyzeFollowUp`): **ORTHOPEDIST / MEDIUM** — *\"Nerve root compression (sciatica or herniated disc)\"*\n479: 5. **Status**: `completed` (resolved in turn 1 — the AI had enough info to triage after one follow-up)\n480: \n481: Second call hit OpenRouter 429 rate limit — expected for demo free-tier. The pipeline works; rate limit is a transient environment constraint, not a code flaw.\n482: \n483: ---\n484: \n485: ## 2026-06-09 — Issue #6: Admin Tools — User Management + Impersonation [COMPLETE]\n486: \n487: **Design grill**: `grill-with-docs` stress-tested against existing infrastructure (ImpersonateResponse type, ENDPOINTS.ADMIN.IMPERSONATE, useAdminUsers hook, AuthProvider, AdminRoute guard, AppLayout).\n488: \n489: **Key design decisions:**\n490: - **sessionStorage + React Context** for impersonation state — survives page refresh without leaking admin's original JWT to disk (sessionStorage auto-clears on tab close)\n491: - **System user blocked on both frontend AND backend** — filtered from users table by email, 403 on controller for `ROLE_SYSTEM`\n492: - **isAdmin and isImpersonating are independent** — admin role retained, just viewing as another user\n493: - **Banner in AppLayout** (outside `<Outlet />`) — visible on all routes, persists across navigation\n494: \n495: ### Changes\n496: \n497: **Backend** (1 file): `ImpersonationController.php`\n498: - Added `AccessDeniedHttpException` import\n499: - After null check: `if (in_array('ROLE_SYSTEM', $user->getRoles(), true))` → 403\n500: \n501: **Frontend** (6 files, 2 new):\n502: \n503: | File | Change |\n504: |------|--------|\n505: | `AuthProvider.tsx` | Added impersonation state — `impersonate(token, email)`, `exitImpersonation()`, sessionStorage for original JWT |\n506: | `ImpersonateButton.tsx` | NEW — TanStack `useMutation`, loading state, navigates to `/triage` on success |\n507: | `UsersTable.tsx` | NEW — queries users via `useAdminUsers`, filters system user, email/roles/created columns, impersonate per row |\n508: | `DashboardPage.tsx` | Users tab replaced placeholder `<p>` with `<UsersTable />` |\n509: | `ImpersonationBanner.tsx` | NEW — amber banner \"Viewing as [email]\" + \"Back to admin\" button |\n510: | `AppLayout.tsx` | Mounted `<ImpersonationBanner />` between Header and main |\n511: \n512: ### Housekeeping (same session)\n513: - `.playwright-mcp/` added to root `.gitignore`\n514: - Hardcoded Chromium path removed from `.opencode/opencode.json`\n515: \n516: ### Verification\n517: \n518: | Check | Status |\n519: |-------|--------|\n520: | `npx tsc --noEmit` | ✅ Clean |\n521: | `pnpm lint` | ✅ Clean (2 pre-existing e2e config errors) |\n522: | `pnpm test` | ✅ 58/60 pass (2 pre-existing poll timing failures) |\n523: | `pnpm build` | ✅ Clean (DashboardPage bundle 9.74kB) |\n524: | PHP lint | ✅ No syntax errors |\n525: \n526: ---\n527: \n528: ## 2026-06-10 — Auth Session + Email Verification + Bugfixes [COMPLETE]\n529: \n530: **Plan**: `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-10-auth-session-email-verification.md`  \n531: **Verification**: Backend 223/223 tests (753 assertions), Frontend 81/81 tests — all pushed\n532: \n533: ### Issue 1: Auth Session Survives DB Reset\n534: \n535: Backend: Created `MeController.php` at `GET /api/me` — returns authenticated user data via `#[CurrentUser]`. Tested 3 cases (200 with JWT, 401 without token, 401 with invalid token).\n536: \n537: Frontend: `AuthProvider` now validates JWT on mount via `GET /api/me`. Added `isLoading` state — initial JWT exp check client-side, then async server validation. On failure: clears all storage (jwt_token, sessionStorage), sets unauthenticated. `ProtectedRoute` shows `<Loader/>` while validating, redirects to `/login` only after validation completes.\n538: \n539: ### Issue 2: Registration Security\n540: \n541: **Password confirmation**: Backend `RegistrationController` validates `password_confirmation` via `Assert\\Collection` + manual mismatch check (422/PASSWORD_MISMATCH). Frontend `RegisterPage` adds \"Confirm Password\" input with client-side match validation.\n542: \n543: **Email verification**: User entity gained `emailVerifiedAt`, `emailVerificationToken` (64-char hex, auto-generated in constructor), `verificationTokenExpiresAt` (+24h). Migration `Version20260610000001.php`. `VerifyEmailController` at `GET /api/verify-email` handles: missing token (400), invalid (404), expired (410), already verified (200), success (200). PUBLIC_ACCESS added to security.yaml.\n544: \n545: **Symfony Mailer**: Installed `symfony/mailer` v7.4.12 (3 deps). MAILER_DSN=smtp://mailpit:1025. Verification email sent on registration (from noreply@triageflow.local via `MailerInterface`, non-fatal try/catch on failure).\n546: \n547: **Login gate**: `EmailVerifiedUserChecker` implements `UserCheckerInterface` — blocks unverified users at login (skips ROLE_ADMIN). Registered on login firewall. Returns \"Please verify your email address before logging in.\" as 401.\n548: \n549: **Mailpit**: Added to docker-compose.yml (axllent/mailpit:latest), SMTP:1025, Web:8025.\n550: \n551: **Frontend**: `VerifyEmailPage.tsx` at `/verify-email?token=xxx` calls backend internally, shows success/failure UI. Login page shows blue info box with Mailpit link after registration, amber warning for unverified login error.\n552: \n553: **DEFAULT_URI**: Changed from `http://localhost` to `http://localhost:5173` in .env, .env.example, setup.sh.\n554: \n555: ### Model Fix\n556: \n557: Default model was `google/gemma-4-31b-it:free`, fallback `openai/gpt-oss-120b:free` was dead config (never referenced in `OpenRouterClient::chat()`). Fixed to switch to fallback on 429 with 2s delay + exponential backoff for network retries. 3 new tests. Later switched default to `openrouter/free` (OpenRouter's meta-router picks best free model) per user direction.\n558: \n559: ### Processing Hang Fix\n560: \n561: No messenger consumer running — `ProcessTriageMessage` and `ProcessSyntheticTurnMessage` piled up in `messenger_messages` table. Fixed by starting consumer (`docker compose exec -d php ... messenger:consume async --time-limit=3600`). Backlog processed (submission `2ca3c6ae` → completed ORTHOPEDIST/MEDIUM). Added consumer start to `bin/setup.sh`.\n562: \n563: ### Messenger Auto-Setup Fix\n564: \n565: `MESSENGER_TRANSPORT_DSN` had `auto_setup=0` — after DB reset, `messenger_messages` table was gone. Changed to `auto_setup=1` so table auto-creates. Added manual SQL setup for existing DB.\n566: \n567: ### Submissions Clickable Fix\n568: \n569: `SubmissionsList.tsx` only showed \"View Result\" link for `status === 'completed'`. Changed to `status !== 'failed'` — non-completed submissions show \"View Details\" link. `TriageResultPage` already handles all statuses. Also removed empty `docs/testing/bugs.md`.\n570: \n571: ### Code Review Fixes\n572: \n573: - `bin/setup.sh:174` — `success` message was unconditional after messenger consumer start (restructured as if/then/else)\n574: - `bin/setup.sh:148` — Mailpit used fixed `sleep 3` instead of retry loop (replaced with 15-retry loop like PostgreSQL check)\n575: - `README.md` — redundant URL text removed\n576: \n577: ### Verification\n578: \n579: | Check | Status |\n580: |-------|--------|\n581: | Backend tests | ✅ 223/223 pass (753 assertions) |\n582: | Frontend tests | ✅ 81/81 pass |\n583: | Full pipeline (register → verify → login → triage submit) | ✅ End-to-end verified |\n584: | OpenRouter rate limiting | ⚠️ 429 on free tier (expected demo limitation) |\n585: \n586: ### Deferred\n587: - OpenRouter rate limiting protection (retry-with-backoff on 429 for both models)\n588: \n589: ---\n590: \n591: ## 2026-06-11 — Story 9: Generate Button + Async Queue [COMPLETE]\n592: \n593: **Frontend**: Added \"Generate Synthetic Case\" button on admin dashboard (`DashboardPage.tsx`) with green success banner. New `useGenerateSyntheticCase.ts` mutation hook (TanStack Query), invalidates admin stats + submissions on success.\n594: \n595: **Backend queue refactor**: `GenerateSyntheticCaseHandler` now dispatches `ProcessSyntheticCaseMessage` for async AI analysis instead of running it inline (was blocking ~4-10s). New `ProcessSyntheticCaseMessageHandler` — loads submission, calls `TriageAnalyzer::analyzeInitial()`, handles result/question/failure. Routed via `messenger.yaml` to async transport.\n596: \n597: **Worker container**: Added `worker` service to `docker-compose.yml` running `messenger:consume async --limit=10`.\n598: \n599: **Bugfix — AI symptom overflow**: AI occasionally ignored the 500-char prompt instruction (generated 1776 chars). Added defense-in-depth truncation (497 chars + `...`) in `generateSymptom()`.\n600: \n601: **Bugfix — Import typo**: `useAdminSubscriptions` → `useAdminSubmissions` in `DashboardPage.tsx`.\n602: \n603: **Verification**: 228 tests, 775 assertions. Docker compose up — worker consuming from async transport. E2E: generate endpoint returns 201, worker processes message (OpenRouter 200 in ~1s). Frontend build passes (171 modules).\n604: \n605: ---\n606: \n607: ## 2026-06-12 — Issue #7: Testing & Polish [COMPLETE]\n608: \n609: **Session**: OpenAgent — full diagnostic + fix cycle\n610: \n611: ### Initial State\n612: - **Backend**: 228 tests, **54 errors** — all caused by `symfony/mailer` not installed (framework.yaml had mailer config, package in composer.json but never in vendor/)\n613: - **Frontend**: 81 tests, **5 failed** — DashboardPage tests rendered `useGenerateSyntheticCase()` (calls `useQueryClient()`) without `QueryClientProvider`\n614: - **PHPStan**: Not installed (missing from composer.json dev-deps)\n615: - **ChatMessage/ConversationBubble**: Zero dedicated tests\n616: - Issue #7 marked `ready-for-agent`, all AC not met\n617: \n618: ### Fix 1 — symfony/mailer\n619: - `composer install` resolved it (was already in composer.lock, just missing from vendor/)\n620: - Result: **228 tests, 0 errors** (resolved all 54)\n621: \n622: ### Fix 2 — DashboardPage tests\n623: - Added `TestWrapper` with `MemoryRouter` + `QueryClientProvider`, used via `render(<Component />, { wrapper: TestWrapper })`\n624: - Result: **81 tests, 0 failures** (resolved all 5)\n625: \n626: ### Fix 3 — PHPStan level 5\n627: - Installed `phpstan/phpstan`, `phpstan/phpstan-symfony`, `phpstan/phpstan-doctrine`, `phpstan/phpstan-phpunit`\n628: - Created `phpstan.neon.dist` with `treatPhpDocTypesAsCertain: false`\n629: - Fixed 40 errors (3 redundant null checks in `TriageAnalyzer.php`, 37 in tests)\n630: - Result: **0 errors at level 5**\n631: \n632: ### Fix 4 — ConversationBubble component test\n633: - 6 tests: user alignment (right), assistant alignment (left), result badge, content rendering, timestamp presence, initial_description alignment\n634: - Result: **87 frontend tests pass (12 files)**\n635: \n636: ### Pushed\n637: | Repo | Head | Message |\n638: |------|------|---------|\n639: | Backend | `4166fe2` | fix(testing): install symfony/mailer, add PHPStan level 5, fix test quality issues |\n640: | Frontend | `25cbdb9` | test(triage): add ConversationBubble component tests — and `affdcaf` for DashboardPage wrapper |\n641: \n642: ### Issue #7 Closed\n643: All 10 acceptance criteria met, issue closed via `gh issue close 7`.\n644: \n645: ---\n646: \n647: ## 2026-06-13 — Issue #10: Structured Logging + Observability [COMPLETE]\n648: \n649: **Session**: OpenAgent — grill → implement → code review → fix → push  \n650: **Verification**: Frontend 95/95 tests, TSC+ESLint clean. Backend 180/180 unit tests, PHPStan level 5 clean. Infrastructure-dependent 45 tests skipped (no PostgreSQL).\n651: \n652: ### Grill Session (`grill-with-docs`, compressed)\n653: \n654: Resolved all design decisions for structured logging:\n655: - **Correlation IDs**: UUID v4 via `Uuid::v4()->toRfc4122()`, static processor (not request-scoped)\n656: - **Subscriber**: HTTP `kernel.request`/`kernel.response` — handlers set own UUID in worker context\n657: - **OpenRouterClient**: `?LoggerInterface $logger = null` (optional, NullLogger in tests)\n658: - **Log field naming**: snake_case for JSON output\n659: - **Monolog processor**: default (all handlers/channels, no restriction)\n660: - **Handler status**: named string per return path (`noop_*`, `analysis_failed`, `success`, `error`)\n661: \n662: ### Backend Implementation\n663: \n664: **New files** (3):\n665: - `src/Shared/Infrastructure/Logging/CorrelationIdProcessor.php` — Monolog processor, `__invoke(LogRecord): LogRecord`, sets `$record->extra['correlation_id']`\n666: - `src/Shared/Infrastructure/Logging/CorrelationIdSubscriber.php` — `#[AsEventListener]` for kernel.request (priority 100, UUID gen) + kernel.response (X-Correlation-Id header)\n667: - `tests/Shared/Infrastructure/Logging/CorrelationIdSubscriberTest.php` — 6 tests (UUID format, sub-request skip, header presence/absence/skip)\n668: \n669: **Modified files** (8):\n670: - `config/services.yaml` — `monolog.processor` tag registration\n671: - `OpenRouterClient.php` — Optional logger with timing, primary-429 warning, retry-notice, rate-limit-all error, token_usage extraction\n672: - `ProcessTriageMessageHandler.php` — LoggerInterface + timing + status tracking\n673: - `ProcessSyntheticCaseMessageHandler.php` — Same, plus terminal state guard\n674: - `ProcessSyntheticTurnMessageHandler.php` — Same, with `failed_empty_answer` naming\n675: - `OpenRouterClientTest.php` — Added `logger: null` to named constructor args\n676: - 2 handler tests — LoggerInterface mock injection\n677: \n678: **Bug found & fixed**: `CorrelationIdProcessor` typed `array $record` but Monolog 3 passes `LogRecord` objects. Changed to `LogRecord` with `$record->extra['correlation_id']` mutation.\n679: \n680: **PHP 8.5 quirk**: Named arguments can't skip optional params before required ones. Moved `$logger` after all required params in `OpenRouterClient` constructor. Also fixed PHPStan `parameter.requiredAfterOptional`.\n681: \n682: ### Frontend Lint Fixes (same session)\n683: \n684: Cleaned 12 ESLint errors across 7 files:\n685: - `AuthProvider.tsx` — Removed redundant JWT expiry checks from `useEffect` (already in `useState` initializer)\n686: - `VerifyEmailPage.tsx` — Moved `!token` early return to `useState` initializer\n687: - `useAdminFailedMessages.ts` / `useGenerateSyntheticCase.ts` — Added `void` to floating `invalidateQueries` promises + typed API response\n688: - `FailedMessagesTable.tsx` — Removed unused import\n689: - `ImpersonateButton.test.tsx` — `eslint-disable` for intentional empty executor\n690: - `eslint.config.js` — Ignored playwright config + e2e specs\n691: \n692: ### Code Review Outcomes\n693: \n694: 5 Important + 1 Minor fixed:\n695: | # | Issue | Fix |\n696: |---|-------|-----|\n697: | 1 | Missing terminal guard in ProcessSyntheticCaseMessageHandler | Added `noop_already_terminal` guard |\n698: | 2 | Missing warning on primary model 429 | Added `$this->logger?->warning(...)` |\n699: | 3 | Missing notice on transport retry success | Conditional notice vs info based on `$attempts > 0` |\n700: | 4 | `empty_answer` naming inconsistent | Renamed → `failed_empty_answer` |\n701: | 5 | `rate_limited_all_models` used warning (spec said error) | Changed to `error` |\n702: | 6 | `$status = 'noop'` unreachable | Changed to defensive `'noop_already_terminal'` |\n703: \n704: ### Commits\n705: \n706: | Repo | Commit | Message |\n707: |------|--------|---------|\n708: | Backend | `fea218d` | feat: add structured logging with correlation IDs |\n709: | Frontend | `3b0a0aa` | fix: resolve ESLint errors across auth, admin hooks, and tests |\n710: \n711: ### Push Status\n712: \n713: | Repo | Remote | Head |\n714: |------|--------|------|\n715: | Backend | `psswid/triageflow-backend` | `fea218d` |\n716: | Frontend | `psswid/triageflow-frontend` | `3b0a0aa` |\n717: | Docs | `psswid/triageflow-docs` | up-to-date |\n718: \n719: ---\n720: \n721: ## 2026-06-12 — CI Pipeline: Backend CI Fixed (5 iterations) [COMPLETE]\n722: \n723: **Two workflow files created** — `backend/.github/workflows/ci.yml` (3 jobs) + `frontend/.github/workflows/ci.yml` (2 jobs).\n724: \n725: **Frontend CI passed immediately** ✅ — Vitest 87 tests + TypeScript typecheck.\n726: \n727: **Backend CI required 5 fixes across 4 commits:**\n728: \n729: | # | Fix | Issue |\n730: |---|-----|-------|\n731: | 1 | `cp .env.test .env` before `composer install` | `.env` missing in CI checkout (gitignored) |\n732: | 2 | `--no-scripts` flag + `.env` creation after install | `cache:clear` auto-script fails without `.env` |\n733: | 3 | `DEFAULT_URI` env var added | Needed by `routing.yaml` + `services.yaml` at boot |\n734: | 4 | `CORS_ALLOW_ORIGIN`, `MESSENGER_TRANSPORT_DSN`, `MAILER_DSN`, `JWT_*` | All needed at runtime, not in `.env.test` |\n735: | 5 | `JWT_PASSPHRASE=` (empty) | OpenSSL 3.x on ubuntu-latest rejects non-empty passphrase on unencrypted PKCS#8 key (`DECODER routines::unsupported`) |\n736: | 6 | `openssl genpkey` in CI | JWT keys not tracked in git — don't exist in checkout |\n737: | 7 | `Length(min: 8)` named args | Symfony 7.3 deprecation triggers `failOnDeprecation=\"true\"` |\n738: | 8 | `coverage: pcov` (was `none`) | \"No coverage driver\" warning triggers `failOnWarning=\"true\"` |\n739: \n740: **Final state**: ✅ All 3 jobs green — 228 tests / 771 assertions in 62s, PHPStan level 5 clean in 16s, Docker build in 42s.\n741: \n742: **ADR-0007 created** — documents the decision to generate JWT keys at runtime in CI rather than committing them.\n743: \n744: ---\n745: \n746: ## 2026-06-12 — Issue #9: Worker Monitoring + Failed Messages [COMPLETE]\n747: \n748: **Plan**: `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-12-failed-messages.md`  \n749: **Verification**: Backend 236/236 tests (797 assertions), Frontend 95/95 tests (13 files), TypeScript zero errors — all merged to `master`\n750: \n751: ### Design Decisions (via `grill-with-docs`)\n752: \n753: | # | Question | Decision |\n754: |---|----------|----------|\n755: | Q1 | Failed Messages vs Dead Letter Queue | **Failed Messages** (aligns with Symfony's `failed` transport) |\n756: | Q2 | HealthController location | Standalone at `App\\Controller` (cross-cutting) |\n757: | Q3 | Retry/Delete approach vs service layer | **Raw SQL** via DBAL\\Connection (matches GET approach) |\n758: | Q4 | FailedMessagesTable pattern | **Self-fetching** (like UsersTable) |\n759: | Q5 | Endpoint location | `AdminController` (not separate controller) |\n760: | Q6 | Tab placement | New \"Failed Messages\" tab (not panel within Overview) |\n761: | Q7a | Data model | `FailedMessageResource` with `preview` (extracted from body) |\n762: | Q7b | Retry/Delete UX | **Inline buttons** (blue Retry + red Delete, confirm dialog) |\n763: | Q7c | Polling interval | **15s** |\n764: \n765: ### Backend Changes\n766: \n767: **AdminController.php** (+100 lines, 3 endpoints):\n768: - `GET /api/admin/failed-messages` — queries `messenger_messages WHERE queue_name = 'failed'`, returns JSON:API-style with type/error/preview/timestamp\n769: - `POST /api/admin/failed-messages/{id}/retry` — **atomic UPDATE** `SET queue_name = 'default', delivered_at = NULL WHERE id = :id AND queue_name = 'failed'`, checks affected row count for 404\n770: - `DELETE /api/admin/failed-messages/{id}` — **atomic DELETE** `WHERE id = :id AND queue_name = 'failed'`, checks affected row count for 404\n771: \n772: Key fixes from code review:\n\n(Output capped at 50 KB. Showing lines 1-772. Use offset=773 to continue.)\n</content>",
