            "output": "<path>/home/stefan/dev/projects/triageflow/docs/handoffs/handoff-2026-06-14-business-website-layer.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Handoff: Business Website Layer — Complete\n2: \n3: **Date:** 2026-06-14\n4: **Branch:** `master` (all 3 repos)\n5: **Repo:** `psswid/triageflow-docs` (parent, incl. `backend/`)  \n6: **Frontend repo:** `psswid/triageflow-frontend`  \n7: **Issue:** `psswid/triageflow-docs#11` — UX Polish (expanded scope)\n8: \n9: ## Session Summary\n10: \n11: Built the full public-facing business website layer on top of the authenticated triage SPA. This was a major expansion of Issue #11 beyond its original UX-polish scope: 7 new marketing/legal pages, i18n (EN+PL), dark mode toggle, cookie consent, design system expansion, and localized backend emails.\n12: \n13: ## What Changed\n14: \n15: Full details in these artifacts instead of duplicating here:\n16: \n17: | Artifact | Location |\n18: |----------|----------|\n19: | Implementation plan | `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-13-business-website-layer.md` |\n20: | Session log | `raw_log.md` (entry: \"2026-06-14 — Business Website Layer\") |\n21: | ADR | `docs/adr/0008-dual-purpose-frontend-architecture.md` |\n22: | Domain glossary update | `CONTEXT.md` — added dual-purpose frontend description |\n23: \n24: ### In Brief\n25: \n26: - **7 new public pages**: Landing (glassmorphism hero, Lucide icons), About (developer profile, Tech Decisions, amber disclaimer), How It Works (vertical timeline), Contact (2×2 social grid), Privacy/Terms/Cookies (all with sticky ToC sidebar)\n27: - **i18n**: `react-i18next` + `i18next-browser-languagedetector`. 16 locale JSON files (8 EN + 8 PL). All 26 existing source components migrated to `useTranslation()`.\n28: - **Dark mode**: `useDarkMode` hook (system pref detection + localStorage persistence) + sun/moon toggle in header & footer. Init in `main.tsx` before `createRoot()` to prevent FOUC.\n29: - **Cookie consent**: Minimal one-click banner, no tracking, persisted in localStorage.\n30: - **Layout architecture**: `MarketingLayout` (public pages) + standalone unauth group (login/register/verify-email) + `AppLayout` (authenticated pages with `ProtectedRoute`/`AdminRoute` wrappers)\n31: - **Design tokens**: Full primary (50-950), accent teal (50-950), surface slate (50-950), urgency, `--font-*`, `--radius-*` tokens added at `@theme` level. Poppins 600/700 via Google Fonts for marketing headings. Lucide icons tree-shakeable.\n32: - **Backend**: `RegistrationController` sends PL verification emails based on `Accept-Language` header.\n33: - **Code review**: All 11 issues resolved (2 Critical, 8 Important, 1 test gap). 146/146 tests, TSC clean, ESLint clean, build passes.\n34: \n35: ### Pre-existing Issues Not Addressed\n36: \n37: - Chunk size warning (535KB main bundle > 500KB)\n38: - E2E Playwright suite can't run under vitest\n39: - 4 ESLint errors in playwright config + e2e specs (pre-existing, outside src/)\n40: - Backend DB functional tests blocked by `pdo_pgsql` driver\n41: - Accessibility audit (original Issue #11 Phase 2 HITL) — not yet performed\n42: \n43: ## Verification (fresh)\n44: \n45: | Check | Result |\n46: |-------|--------|\n47: | `npx tsc --noEmit` | ✅ Clean |\n48: | `npx eslint src/` | ✅ 0 errors, 0 warnings |\n49: | `npx vitest run` | ✅ 146/146 pass (24 files) |\n50: | `npx vite build` | ✅ Exit 0 (1969 modules, 239ms) |\n51: | `php -l RegistrationController.php` | ✅ No syntax errors |\n52: \n53: ## Suggested Skills for Next Session\n54: \n55: - **`ui-ux-pro-max`** → If running the accessibility audit. Load before reviewing any page for WCAG/ARIA compliance.\n56: - **`brainstorming`** → Before any UX changes that affect interaction patterns.\n57: - **`requesting-code-review`** → Before merging any accessibility fixes.\n58: - **`handoff`** → To save another handoff when the audit is complete.\n\n(End of file - total 58 lines)\n</content>",
